t["subzone:cathedral-square"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,300,17.492.0,26.571.0,25.241.0,31.201.0,36.216.0,33.205.0",["h"]="e53d6a",["n"]="Plaza de la Catedral",["s"]="Plaza de la Catedral. La Plaza de la Catedral es el corazón cívico y espiritual de la Ciudad de Ventormenta, presidido por la majestuosa Catedral de la Luz. Más allá de servir como lugar de culto y devoción, esta animada plaza alberga instituciones municipales como el ayuntamiento, el orfanato de la ciudad y el cuartel general regional del Alba Argenta. Situada al noroeste del Distrito de Mercaderes y al sureste del Distrito de los Enanos, Plaza de la Catedral sirve como el epicentro de la fe en el Reino de Ventormenta. Dominando el horizonte se alza la Catedral de la Luz, el santuario preeminente para los devotos de la Luz Sagrada en todo Azeroth. Sacerdotes, paladines y sanadores se reúnen aquí para estudiar, orar y entrenar. Ciudadanos, peregrinos y escolares locales guiados por la Maestra de escuela Danna se mezclan habitualmente en la plaza para conversar y meditar.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Paladin"]="For paladins, Cathedral Square is the fountainhead of faith and duty, housing mentors, sacred vows, and specialized armorers tailored to holy warriors.",["class:Priest"]="The quiet halls and towering spires of the square offer priests a tranquil sanctuary to commune with the Holy Light, advance their spiritual studies, and minister to the citizens of Stormwind."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Cathedral Square is a major district in Stormwind City centered on the Cathedral of Light. It serves as both the spiritual hub for practitioners of the Light and a vital civic center housing City Hall, the local orphanage, and various shops.",["al"]={"cathedral district","holy district","what is this place"},["q"]="What is Cathedral Square?"},{["a"]="Priests and Paladins of the Alliance come to Cathedral Square and the Cathedral of Light to hone their skills and study sacred doctrines. Medics and caregivers also study here under First Aid trainers.",["al"]={"class trainers here","who trains here","paladin priest trainers"},["q"]="Who trains in Cathedral Square?"},{["a"]="The Argent Dawn maintains a prominent embassy in Cathedral Square to recruit able-bodied champions and coordinate logistical support from Stormwind for their relentless crusade against the Scourge in the Plaguelands.",["al"]={"argent dawn stormwind","argent dawn presence"},["q"]="Why is the Argent Dawn located here?"},{["a"]="Bridges and canal paths link Cathedral Square directly to the bustling Trade District to the southeast, the industrial Dwarven District to the northwest, and the quiet gardens of the Park to the southwest.",["al"]={"connected districts","where does this go"},["q"]="Where does Cathedral Square lead?"}},["kw"]={"argent dawn","cathedral of light","cathedral square","city hall","holy district","orphanage","paladin","priest","stormwind"},["n"]="Cathedral Square",["s"]="Cathedral Square is the spiritual and civic heart of Stormwind City, dominated by the majestic Cathedral of Light. Beyond serving as a place of worship and devotion, the bustling plaza houses municipal institutions like City Hall, the city orphanage, and the regional headquarters of the Argent Dawn.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Situated northwest of the Trade District and southeast of the Dwarven District, Cathedral Square serves as the epicenter of faith in the Kingdom of Stormwind. Dominating the skyline is the Cathedral of Light, the preeminent sanctuary for followers of the Holy Light across Azeroth. Priests, paladins, and healers gather here to study, pray, and train. Citizens, pilgrims, and local schoolchildren led by School Mistress Danna regularly mingle in the square for conversation and contemplation.",["t"]="The Holy District"},{["b"]="The district is not merely reserved for prayer; it is one of the capital's busiest civic centers. The square houses the Stormwind Orphanage as well as City Hall, anchoring the administrative life of the kingdom. Specialized armorers and weaponsmiths catering to holy crusaders, such as Righteous Plates and Just Maces, line the avenues. It also serves as the base of operations for the Argent Dawn within Stormwind, where recruiters and representatives coordinate relief efforts and rally champions against the encroaching threats of the Scourge in the northern kingdoms.",["t"]="Civic Heart and Holy Order"}}}}}
t["subzone:cavern-of-mists"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,268,30.540.0,29.223.0,37.134.0,25.180.0,26.141.0",["h"]="66dec1",["n"]="Caverna de las Brumas",["s"]="Caverna de las Brumas. La Caverna de las Brumas es la amplia antecámara exterior que conduce a las profundidades de las Cuevas de los Lamentos. Alimentada por géiseres subterráneos que brotan a través de la roca, su poza central y su densa niebla albergan una extraña fauna mutada que merodea justo fuera del umbral del portal. Antes de descender al verdadero corazón de las Cuevas de los Lamentos, los viajeros deben abrirse paso por la Caverna de las Brumas. Un vapor denso y cálido flota permanentemente en el aire, alimentado por géiseres naturales que brotan del suelo de la caverna hacia una profunda poza central. Aunque sirve como entrada, dista mucho de ser un lugar apacible. Manadas de raptores, serpientes, mocos y trilladones semiacuáticos deambulan por las cornisas y las aguas, junto a bestias tristemente célebres como la hidra Trigore el Azotador. Ofrece a los aventureros un sombrío anticipo del crecimiento antinatural que se corrompe en las profundidades.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="The twisted wildlife thriving in the heavy vapors gives Cenarion druids their first warning of how deeply Naralex's Emerald Dream communion has gone astray.",["faction:Horde"]="Resting right in the heart of the Barrens, clearing out the predatory beasts lurking in these mists is critical to securing the trade routes and outposts around the Crossroads."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Cavern of Mists comprises the outer cave system of the Wailing Caverns, located southwest of the Crossroads in the Barrens. It is the non-instanced chamber that players must traverse to reach the instance portal itself.",["al"]={"cavern of mists location","where is cavern of mists","wailing caverns entrance cave"},["q"]="Where is the Cavern of Mists?"},{["a"]="Active geysers constantly burst from the stone floor, feeding the central pool and filling the subterranean air with heavy, humid fog.",["al"]={"why misty","cavern of mists name origin"},["q"]="Why is it called the Cavern of Mists?"},{["a"]="The chamber is populated by raptors, oozes, wind serpents, snakes, toads, and threshadons inhabiting the pool, as well as occasional sightings of the rare hydra Trigore the Lasher.",["al"]={"mobs in cavern of mists","cavern of mists monsters"},["q"]="What creatures live here?"},{["a"]="Trigore the Lasher is a dangerous rare hydra that can occasionally be found swimming alongside the threshadons in the chamber's central pool.",["al"]={"trigore","hydra rare wailing caverns"},["q"]="Who is Trigore the Lasher?"}},["kw"]={"barrens","cavern of mists","geysers","threshadons","trigore the lasher","wailing caverns"},["n"]="Cavern of Mists",["s"]="The Cavern of Mists is the expansive outer antechamber leading into the depths of the Wailing Caverns. Fed by subterranean geysers that erupt through the rock, its central pool and hanging fog harbor strange, mutated wildlife roaming just outside the portal threshold.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Before descending into the true heart of the Wailing Caverns, travelers must navigate the Cavern of Mists. Thick, warm vapor hangs permanently in the air, fed by natural geysers erupting from the cavern floor into a deep central pool. Though it serves as an entryway, it is far from peaceful. Swarms of raptors, serpents, oozes, and semi-aquatic threshadons wander the ledges and waters, alongside notorious beasts like the hydra Trigore the Lasher. It provides adventurers an ominous preview of the unnatural growth festering deeper below.",["t"]="The Threshold of the Nightmare"}}}}}
t["subzone:cenarion-enclave"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,358,19.640.0,21.376.0,31.283.0,24.246.0,35.227.0,57.362.0",["h"]="70de06",["n"]="Enclave Cenarion",["s"]="Enclave Cenarion. El Enclave Cenarion es el frondoso distrito noroccidental de Darnassus, que ejerce de lugar de reunión central y sede de poder para el Círculo Cenarion en la capital. Mientras el archidruida Malfurión Tempestira yace sumido en el Sueño Esmeralda, el archidruida Fandral Corzocelada lidera a los druidas elfos de la noche desde los grandes huecos y ramas vivas de este bosque. Ubicado en una alta terraza sobre Los Jardines del Templo, el Enclave Cenarion está esculpido a partir de antiguos robles y fresnos marcados con cortezas rúnicas. Las asambleas del Círculo Cenarion se reúnen en el interior de estructuras moldeadas directamente a partir de madera viva y piedra. Con Malfurión Tempestira ausente en el Sueño Esmeralda, el archidruida Fandral Corzocelada supervisa los asuntos de este lugar, promoviendo su ambiciosa visión para Teldrassil a pesar de la constante fricción política con la suma sacerdotisa Tyrande Susurravientos. Más allá de los druidas que meditan entre sus arroyos, el enclave también acoge a los cazadores elfos de la capital y los establos donde los jinetes consumados aprenden a domesticar a los sables de la noche de Darnassus.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="For night elf druids, the Cenarion Enclave is the civil center of your order on Teldrassil, offering training and guidance under the stern direction of Archdruid Fandral Staghelm.",["class:Hunter"]="Hunters gather in the enclave's eastern boughs to hone their marksmanship and wilderness lore alongside beastmasters who rear the capital's nightsabers."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Archdruid Fandral Staghelm currently leads the grove and the night elven druids residing in Darnassus. Malfurion Stormrage, the supreme leader of the Cenarion Circle, remains trapped in a deep, unexplained slumber within the Emerald Dream, leaving Staghelm as the de facto authority.",["al"]={"who is in charge here","cenarion enclave leader","fandral staghelm"},["q"]="Who leads the Cenarion Enclave?"},{["a"]="The enclave is the primary home of the capital's druid trainers, who instruct novices among the living trees. Eastern boughs house the city's hunter trainers, while the root warrens beneath the western bough shelter a quiet den of rogue trainers.",["al"]={"trainers in cenarion enclave","druid trainer darnassus","hunter trainer darnassus"},["q"]="What classes train here?"},{["a"]="Riding trainers and breeders tending to Darnassus's prized saber cats are stationed at the base of the eastern tree near the grove's entrance, providing both riding training and nightsaber mounts to eligible Alliance travelers.",["al"]={"nightsaber trainer","night elf mount trainer","darnassus riding trainer"},["q"]="Where can I buy a nightsaber mount?"},{["a"]="While this district lies within an Alliance capital and is led by the staunchly nationalist Fandral Staghelm, the Cenarion Circle as a broader organization remains dedicated to safeguarding the natural order rather than fighting factional wars. However, the presence of Staghelm makes this particular enclave strongly aligned with night elven regional interests.",["al"]={"is cenarion circle alliance","are druids alliance only"},["q"]="What is the Cenarion Circle's stance toward the Alliance?"}},["kw"]={"cenarion circle","cenarion enclave","darnassus","druid","fandral staghelm","nightsaber","teldrassil"},["n"]="Cenarion Enclave",["s"]="The Cenarion Enclave is the verdant northwestern district of Darnassus, serving as the central gathering place and seat of power for the Cenarion Circle in the capital. While Archdruid Malfurion Stormrage lies slumbering within the Emerald Dream, Archdruid Fandral Staghelm leads the night elven druids from the great hollows and living boughs of this grove.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Occupying a high terrace above the Temple Gardens, the Cenarion Enclave is shaped from ancient oaks and ashes marked with runic bark. Convocations of the Cenarion Circle gather within structures molded directly from living wood and stone. With Malfurion Stormrage absent in the Emerald Dream, Archdruid Fandral Staghelm oversees affairs here, pushing his ambitious vision for Teldrassil despite lingering political friction with High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind. Beyond the druids who meditate among its streams, the enclave also hosts the capital's elven hunters and the stables where skilled riders learn to tame Darnassian nightsabers.",["t"]="Heart of the Circle"},{["b"]="Though renowned as a tranquil sanctuary of nature, the enclave harbors more covert activities. Beneath the hollowed roots of the westernmost bough lies a subterranean refuge used by Darnassus's clandestine rogues, who conduct their quiet business shielded by the rustling canopy above. Druidic elders tolerate this presence, provided the balance of the grove is not disturbed.",["t"]="Shadows in the Boughs"}}}}}
t["subzone:champions-hall"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,396,31.625.0,37.124.0,42.230.0,35.212.0,46.154.0",["h"]="b27d18",["n"]="Sala de los Campeones",["s"]="Sala de los Campeones. Escondida en los confines meridionales del Casco Antiguo, la Sala de los Campeones sirve como cuartel de oficiales y armería de suministros para los veteranos condecorados de la Alianza en Ventormenta. Tras cruzar su umbral, los intendentes proporcionan armas especializadas, armaduras de placas y distintivos a los guerreros consagrados de la facción. El acceso está estrictamente custodiado y reservado únicamente para aquellos oficiales que hayan demostrado su valor en el campo de batalla. Oculta tras una entrada vigilada en el Casco Antiguo, la Sala de los Campeones es un refugio exclusivo para los combatientes más distinguidos de la Alianza. Los mandos militares se reúnen aquí ante mapas tácticos de Azeroth para deliberar sobre las campañas en curso, rodeados de armamento y las insignias honoríficas de su rango. Solo aquellos soldados que hayan ascendido en la jerarquía militar de la Alianza hasta alcanzar el estatus de oficial —concretamente el rango de Knight o superior— tienen permitida la entrada. En su interior, los intendentes militares suministran a los curtidos soldados armas de élite, armaduras y monturas fabricadas expresamente para decantar la balanza contra la Horda en los territorios en disputa de todo el mundo.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Warrior"]="For front-line combatants, the hall represents the ultimate military stockpile, offering heavy battle gear and armaments reserved only for proven battlefield leaders.",["faction:Alliance"]="The hall stands as the premier symbol of Alliance military merit in Stormwind, honoring those who dedicate their lives to repelling Horde incursions."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Champions' Hall is located in the southern section of Old Town in Stormwind City, tucked away behind a guarded entrance.",["al"]={"where is champions hall","pvp vendor stormwind location","how to find champions hall"},["q"]="Where is the Champions' Hall located?"},{["a"]="Only Alliance veterans who have earned the military rank of Knight (Rank 6) or higher through the faction's honor system are granted passage through the entrance portal. Unproven recruits and civilians are barred at the threshold.",["al"]={"can anyone enter","champions hall requirements","why cant i enter champions hall"},["q"]="Who is allowed inside the Champions' Hall?"},{["a"]="The hall contains quartermasters offering officer-tier weapons, armor, insignia, and specialized war mounts. Alliance tacticians and generals also congregate around war tables lined with regional maps of Azeroth.",["al"]={"what does champions hall have","what vendors are in champions hall","champions hall rewards"},["q"]="What is inside the Champions' Hall?"},{["a"]="The Horde counterpart is the Hall of Legends, situated in Orgrimmar, which provides identical military supply services to decorated warriors of the Horde.",["al"]={"horde version of champions hall","orgrimmar pvp room","horde pvp barracks"},["q"]="What is the Horde equivalent of this building?"}},["kw"]={"champions hall","grand marshal","knight","officer barracks","old town","pvp vendors","quartermaster","stormwind"},["n"]="Champions' Hall",["s"]="Tucked away in the southern reaches of Old Town, the Champions' Hall serves as the officer's barracks and supply armory for the Alliance's decorated veterans in Stormwind. Beyond its threshold, quartermasters dispense specialized weapons, plate, and regalia to proven warriors of the faction. Access is strictly guarded, reserved only for officers who have demonstrated valor on the field of war.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Hidden behind a guarded threshold in Old Town, the Champions' Hall is a restricted haven for the Alliance's most distinguished combatants. Military commanders gather here over tactical maps of Azeroth to confer on ongoing campaigns, flanked by armaments and the grand insignias of rank. Only soldiers who have climbed the Alliance hierarchy to achieve officer status—specifically the rank of Knight or higher—are permitted entry. Inside, military quartermasters supply battle-hardened soldiers with elite arms, armor, and mounts crafted specifically to turn the tide against the Horde in contested zones across the world.",["t"]="The Alliance Officer's Barracks"}}}}}
t["subzone:charred-vale"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="12,275,19.499.0,20.411.0,32.249.0,48.216.0,40.172.0,50.122.0",["h"]="d2ebe8",["n"]="La Vega Carbonizada",["s"]="La Vega Carbonizada. La Vega Carbonizada es un valle humeante en el suroeste de Sierra Espolón, devastado por la tala imprudente y la maquinaria de Ventura y Cía. Antaño un próspero refugio para antárboles y quimeras, ahora está envuelto en llamas, elementales errantes y arpías hostiles. No hace mucho tiempo, esta cuenca del suroeste era un floreciente bosque alpino custodiado por majestuosos antárboles y habitado por quimeras y arpías autóctonas. Su ruina comenzó con la llegada de Ventura y Cía. La codiciosa organización de goblins taló por completo el bosque con maquinaria explosiva, corrompiendo a los guardianes y despertando a caóticos elementales de fuego. Aunque los antárboles acabaron haciendo retroceder a los goblins, la tierra quedó quebrantada, marcada por el fuego y mancillada por los viles artefactos que desplegaron los leñadores en su retirada.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="The devastation here serves as a harsh warning of what happens when natural balance is shattered by uncontrolled greed, making the valley a key focus for reclamation efforts.",["faction:Horde"]="Operating out of Sun Rock Retreat, Horde forces work closely with Cenarion allies to contain the elemental unrest and push back the corruptive lingering aftermath of the Venture Company."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The devastation was caused by the Venture Company's ruthless logging operations. Their destructive machinery and aggressive deforestation enraged the primal spirits of the land and unleashed destructive fire elementals that spread across the valley.",["al"]={"why is it burning","who burned charred vale","what happened to charred vale"},["q"]="Why is the Charred Vale on fire?"},{["a"]="Tauren druids from nearby Sun Rock Retreat believe it can. They task travelers with soothing the maddened treants and planting enchanted earthen seeds amidst the ash, hoping to coax green shoots from the ruined soil.",["al"]={"is charred vale healing","druids charred vale"},["q"]="Can the forest in the Charred Vale ever recover?"},{["a"]="The basin is crawling with hostile elemental fire spirits, blackened and vengeful ancients, Scorched Basilisks, and wild chimaeras. It is also plagued by Bloodfury harpies.",["al"]={"monsters in charred vale","what lives in charred vale"},["q"]="What creatures inhabit the Charred Vale?"},{["a"]="Its original name has been lost to time, but it was renowned as a lush woodland sanctuary long before goblin axes arrived.",["al"]={"charred vale old name","original name of charred vale"},["q"]="What was the Charred Vale called before it burned?"}},["kw"]={"blackened ancient","bloodfury","charred vale","chimaera","fire elemental","stonetalon","sun rock retreat","venture company"},["n"]="Charred Vale",["s"]="The Charred Vale is a smoldering valley in southwestern Stonetalon Mountains, devastated by the reckless deforestation and machinery of the Venture Company. Once a thriving haven for treants and chimaeras, it is now engulfed in flames, roving elementals, and hostile harpies.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Not long ago, this southwest basin was a flourishing alpine wood guarded by majestic treants and inhabited by native chimaeras and harpies. Its ruin began with the arrival of the Venture Company. The greedy goblin outfit clear-cut the forest with explosive machinery, corrupting the guardians and awakening chaotic fire elementals. Though the treants eventually forced the goblins back, the land was left broken, scarred by fire, and tainted by whatever foul devices the retreating loggers deployed.",["t"]="A Scorched Woodland"},{["b"]="Today, blackened ancients wander blindly through smoke and ash alongside enraged elementals. Bloodfury harpies roost in the skeletal snags, defending what remains of their territory. Despite the hostility of the valley, druids from Sun Rock Retreat refuse to abandon the region, dispatching travelers to sow enchanted seeds and tend the corrupted ancients in a persistent campaign to reclaim the scorched earth.",["t"]="Struggles of Renewal"}}}}}
t["subzone:chill-breeze-valley"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="19,303,30.543.0,37.192.0,49.302.0,42.178.0",["h"]="8aa9bd",["n"]="Valle Escalofrío",["s"]="Valle Escalofrío. El Valle Escalofrío es un paso escarpado y cubierto de nieve situado en el oeste de Dun Morogh que conecta el asentamiento enano de Kharanos con la asediada ciudad de Gnomeregan. Aunque su camino principal es una vía muy transitada por jóvenes viajeros y refugiados, sus apartados rincones albergan peligrosas bestias y sangrientas guaridas. El Valle Escalofrío forma una trinchera en forma de T a través de las montañas del oeste de Dun Morogh. El sendero principal de este a oeste registra un tránsito constante de enanos y gnomos novatos que viajan entre Kharanos y las afueras de Gnomeregan. Sin embargo, adentrarse en la ramificación norte-sur del valle es un asunto completamente diferente. Repletas de manchas de sangre y cadáveres destrozados, estas sombrías zonas albergan feroces depredadores, sobre todo salvajes wendigos que anidan en profundas cuevas de hielo y cazan a cualquiera lo bastante imprudente como para adentrarse en sus cotos de caza.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["race:Dwarf"]="Mountaineers and young dwarven hunters test their mettle clearing out the ferocious wendigos that menace the vital passage connecting central Dun Morogh to the western highlands.",["race:Gnome"]="For gnomish refugees fleeing the fallout of Gnomeregan toward the safety of Kharanos and Ironforge, surviving the trek through Chill Breeze Valley's predatory perimeter is a critical first step."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Chill Breeze Valley is situated in western Dun Morogh, positioned directly between the bustling mountain hub of Kharanos to the east and the technological gnome city of Gnomeregan to the west.",["al"]={"chill breeze valley location","where is chill breeze valley","chill breeze valley map"},["q"]="Where is Chill Breeze Valley located?"},{["a"]="While the main path between Kharanos and Gnomeregan is relatively safe and heavily traveled, the northern and southern offshoots of the valley are hunting grounds for predatory beasts. The snow there is stained with blood and torn carcasses, leading to caves inhabited by vicious, territorial wendigos.",["al"]={"chill breeze valley monsters","dangers in chill breeze valley","why are there bones here"},["q"]="Why is the valley so dangerous to travel through?"},{["a"]="The deeper recesses of the valley are home to ferocious wendigos, including particularly large and elite alpha beasts that have claimed several cave dens as their personal lairs.",["al"]={"wendigo in chill breeze valley","what lives in chill breeze valley"},["q"]="What kinds of beasts make their dens here?"}},["kw"]={"caves","chill breeze valley","dun morogh","gnomeregan","kharanos","t-shaped","wendigo"},["n"]="Chill Breeze Valley",["s"]="Chill Breeze Valley is a rugged, snow-covered pass in western Dun Morogh linking the dwarven settlement of Kharanos with the embattled city of Gnomeregan. While its main path is a well-traveled thoroughfare for young travelers and refugees, its secluded recesses harbor dangerous beasts and bloody dens.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Chill Breeze Valley forms a T-shaped trench through the mountains of western Dun Morogh. The main east-west trail sees steady foot traffic from novice dwarves and gnomes journeying between Kharanos and the outskirts of Gnomeregan. However, straying into the valley's north-south offshoot is another matter entirely. Strewn with bloodstains and mangled carcasses, these shadowy reaches harbor ferocious predators—most notably savage wendigos that lair in deep ice caves and prey on anyone reckless enough to wander into their hunting grounds.",["t"]="A Crossroads of Snow and Claws"}}}}}
t["subzone:cleft-of-shadow"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,315,24.573.0,21.326.0,50.318.0,69.162.0,49.191.0",["h"]="42dc95",["n"]="Circo de las Sombras",["s"]="Circo de las Sombras. Oculto en las profundidades de las cavernas subterráneas bajo Orgrimmar, Circo de las Sombras alberga a quienes practican el sigilo, la hechicería y la demonología en la ciudad. Lejos del orgulloso espíritu guerrero de los distritos superiores de Thrall, sirve como un refugio necesario para pícaros, brujos y magos que operan en las sombras de la Horda. Aunque la nueva Horda de Thrall defiende el honor, el chamanismo y la fuerza de las armas, un liderazgo práctico exige un lugar para artes más sutiles. Excavado en las húmedas cavernas de piedra bajo la capital, Circo de las Sombras acoge a la Hermandad Shadowswift de pícaros, al Enclave Darkfire de brujos y a los eruditos del Enclave Arcano. Apartado del ajetreo diario de los distritos del valle, este sombrío barrio permite a quienes manejan venenos, energía vil y magia arcana ejercer sus oficios lejos de la vista pública directa, mientras permanecen bajo la atenta mirada de los líderes de Orgrimmar.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Rogue"]="The Shadowswift Brotherhood gathers here alongside poison merchants and lockpickers, turning this dark recess into the primary den for the Horde's stealth operatives.",["class:Warlock"]="The Darkfire Enclave gives Horde warlocks a sanctioned place to summon demons and bind fel energy beneath Orgrimmar without drawing the immediate wrath of shaman and warriors."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Thrall strives to keep the Horde united under honorable shamanic and warrior traditions. While the utility of warlocks and rogues is acknowledged, their practices are distrusted by much of the orcish public. Confining them to the subterranean caverns keeps dangerous fel and illicit activities contained and monitored.",["al"]={"why cleft of shadow","why warlocks underground orgrimmar","cleft of shadow lore"},["q"]="Why are warlocks and rogues kept underground here?"},{["a"]="The cavern serves as Orgrimmar's primary hub for rogue, warlock, and mage trainers. It also hosts poison suppliers, reagent vendors, and wand and staff merchants.",["al"]={"trainers in cleft of shadow","who is in cleft of shadow"},["q"]="What major trainers and services can be found in the Cleft of Shadow?"},{["a"]="The chasm plunging into the cavern floor leads to Ragefire Chasm, a perilous subterranean network of lava tubes beneath Orgrimmar infested with troggs, searing elementals, and rogue cultists.",["al"]={"dungeon in cleft of shadow","cleft cave entrance","what instance is here"},["q"]="What is the entrance at the bottom of the cavern?"}},["kw"]={"arcane enclave","cleft of shadow","darkfire enclave","mage","orgrimmar","ragefire chasm","rogue","shadowswift brotherhood","warlock"},["n"]="Cleft of Shadow",["s"]="Tucked deep within the subterranean caverns beneath Orgrimmar, the Cleft of Shadow houses the city's practitioners of stealth, sorcery, and demonology. Far from the proud warrior ethos of Thrall's upper districts, it serves as a necessary haven for rogues, warlocks, and mages operating in the shadows of the Horde.",["sec"]={{["b"]="While Thrall's new Horde champions honor, shamanism, and strength of arms, practical leadership demands a place for subtler arts. Carved into the damp stone caverns below the capital, the Cleft of Shadow hosts the Shadowswift Brotherhood of rogues, the Darkfire Enclave of warlocks, and the scholars of the Arcane Enclave. Kept away from the everyday bustle of the valley districts, this dark quarter allows practitioners of poison, fel energy, and arcane magic to ply their trades out of direct public view while remaining under the watchful eye of Orgrimmar's leadership.",["t"]="A Subterranean Sanctuary"},{["b"]="Beyond acting as a center for covert instruction and magical reagents, the Cleft of Shadow descends directly into Ragefire Chasm. This fiery network of volcanic caves honeycombs beneath Orgrimmar itself, posing an ongoing security threat that draws adventurous defenders and sinister cultists alike right to the cavern's edge.",["t"]="A Dangerous Threshold"}}}}}
t["subzone:cliffspring-falls"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="17,417,16.682.0,26.197.0,49.225.0,42.181.0,51.218.0",["h"]="d3665f",["n"]="Salto de Fonrroca",["s"]="Salto de Fonrroca. El Salto de Fonrroca marca el espectacular origen del vital Río Fonrroca de Costa Oscura, precipitándose desde los acantilados orientales hacia el bosque costero. Celebrado durante mucho tiempo como la principal fuente de agua potable limpia para la región, sus aguas han sido víctimas recientemente de una vil y expansiva corrupción. La caverna subterránea que alimenta la cascada se ha infestado de hostiles nagas y sombríos cultores del Martillo Crepuscular. Brotando de cavernas encaramadas a gran altura en los riscos rocosos del borde oriental de Costa Oscura, el Salto de Fonrroca alimenta el Río Fonrroca, que serpentea hacia el oeste a través de los bosques hasta desembocar en el mar. Tradicionalmente, esta cascada proporcionaba el agua potable más pura para los asentamientos locales de elfos de la noche. En tiempos recientes, sin embargo, las aguas se han vuelto fétidas y turbias, propagando la enfermedad y el deterioro ecológico por toda la cuenca del río. Los naturalistas que investigan el suceso han descubierto que la red de cuevas en la cabecera de las cataratas está invadida por viles nagas y oscuros cultores, que conspiran entre las sombras mientras la corrupción demoníaca del vecino Frondavil amenaza con filtrarse a través del lecho rocoso de las tierras altas.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="Druids of the Cenarion Circle monitor the river closely, striving to diagnose and cleanse the unnatural rot that threatens to choke the wilderness.",["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei of Auberdine, the corruption of Cliffspring Falls is an environmental and spiritual crisis, polluting the vital waters that nourish Darkshore's ancient forests."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Cliffspring Falls is a major waterfall in eastern Darkshore that forms the headwaters of the Cliffspring River. It historically supplied the primary fresh drinking water for the surrounding forest.",["al"]={"cliffspring falls","cliffwater falls","what is cliffspring falls"},["q"]="What is Cliffspring Falls?"},{["a"]="Two sinister influences are suspected: demonic taint seeping through the mountains from corrupted Felwood, and the active presence of Twilight's Hammer cultists and hostile naga lurking inside the caverns feeding the cascade.",["al"]={"why is water tainted","cliffspring river corruption","corrupted water"},["q"]="Why is the water coming from the falls corrupted?"},{["a"]="The caverns above and behind the waterfall are infested with hostile naga slithering through the flooded chambers, alongside cultists belonging to the apocalyptic Twilight's Hammer.",["al"]={"who is in the caves","cliffspring cave mobs","who lives in cliffspring falls"},["q"]="Who occupies the caverns behind the falls?"},{["a"]="The Cliffspring River cuts through the center of northern Darkshore. Because it serves as the principal source of fresh water, its poisoning directly endangers wildlife, ancient groves, and local night elf habitations.",["al"]={"why does darkshore care","cliffspring importance"},["q"]="Why is Cliffspring Falls so important to Darkshore?"}},["kw"]={"auberdine","cliffspring falls","cliffspring river","cliffwater falls","darkshore","felwood","naga","twilight's hammer","water corruption"},["n"]="Cliffspring Falls",["s"]="Cliffspring Falls marks the dramatic origin of Darkshore's vital Cliffspring River, tumbling down from the eastern cliffs into the coastal forest. Long celebrated as the principal source of clean drinking water for the region, its waters have recently fallen victim to a foul, spreading taint. The subterranean cavern feeding the waterfall has become infested with hostile naga and shadowy Twilight's Hammer cultists.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Pouring out from caverns perched high in the rocky bluffs along Darkshore's eastern border, Cliffspring Falls feeds the Cliffspring River, which winds westward across the woods to empty into the sea. Traditionally, this cascade provided the purest drinking water for local night elf settlements. In recent times, however, the waters have turned foul and murky, spreading sickness and ecological decay throughout the river basin. Investigating naturalists have discovered that the cave network at the falls' headwaters is overrun by vile naga and dark cultists, who plot in the shadows while demonic corruption from neighboring Felwood threatens to seep through the highland bedrock.",["t"]="A Tainted Source"}}}}}
t["subzone:cold-hearth-manor"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="17,390,16.513.0,43.236.0,35.230.0,33.229.0,44.297.0",["h"]="aad4cb",["n"]="Mansión Fríogar",["s"]="Mansión Fríogar. La Mansión Fríogar es una granja asolada ubicada justo al oeste de Rémol, junto al camino principal de Claros de Tirisfal. Antaño una finca bulliciosa y hospitalaria conocida por sus abundantes cosechas, el brote de la Plaga de la Muerte aniquiló a sus residentes, dejando los campos circundantes plagados de miembros de la Plaga sin mente. En la actualidad, los Renegados han asegurado la casa de campo principal como puesto de avanzada y parada para los viajeros. Antes de la Tercera Guerra, esta granja gozaba de una reputación de calidez y hospitalidad, produciendo ricas cosechas en el corazón de Lordaeron. Cuando la Plaga arrasó el reino, la familia entera y sus trabajadores sucumbieron, alzándose de nuevo como cascarones atados a la Plaga. Aunque los muertos vivientes ferales todavía deambulan por los campos en ruinas, las fuerzas de los Renegados lograron expulsar a los muertos sin mente de la casa de campo principal, recuperando la estructura para que sirviera como puesto comercial y punto de apoyo a lo largo del camino hacia los claros del este.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="The manor offers a secure vantage along the road between Brill and the eastern reaches of Tirisfal, providing a safe waypoint for travelers navigating the plagued countryside.",["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, reclaiming places like Cold Hearth Manor is a bitter reminder of their lost mortal lives, converting former human sanctuaries into grim defensive outposts against both the Scourge and the Scarlet Crusade."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The farmers and workers who tended the estate were completely wiped out when the Plague of Undeath swept across Lordaeron. Rather than finding peace in death, they were raised as mindless zombies that still haunt the surrounding fields.",["al"]={"who lived at cold hearth","manor backstory","what happened to the family"},["q"]="What happened to the people who lived here?"},{["a"]="The estate originally had a reputation for its warm atmosphere and welcoming fires. The grim moniker was likely adopted by the Forsaken as an ironic nod to its former life, marking how cold, dead, and blighted the farm has become.",["al"]={"cold hearth name meaning","why cold hearth"},["q"]="Why is it called Cold Hearth Manor?"},{["a"]="The Forsaken have taken control of the primary farmhouse, using it as a safe stop for travelers and traders along the road from Brill. However, the open fields and barns surrounding the manor remain infested with hostile Scourge.",["al"]={"who owns cold hearth manor","is cold hearth friendly"},["q"]="Who controls the manor right now?"},{["a"]="The Forsaken in Tirisfal Glades are stretched thin, fighting off mindless Scourge remnants while warding off Scarlet Crusade crusaders. Securing the farmhouse and main road provides immediate utility, leaving the scattered dead in the fields as a nuisance rather than an immediate threat to Brill.",["al"]={"why are there zombies in the fields","why scourge here"},["q"]="Why don't the Forsaken clear out the fields?"}},["kw"]={"brill","cold hearth manor","farmstead","forsaken","scourge","tirisfal glades","zombies"},["n"]="Cold Hearth Manor",["s"]="Cold Hearth Manor is a blighted farmstead located just west of Brill along the main road of Tirisfal Glades. Once a bustling, hospitable estate known for bountiful crops, the outbreak of the Plague of Undeath wiped out its residents, leaving the surrounding fields choked with mindless Scourge. Today, the Forsaken have secured the main farmhouse as an outpost and waystation for travelers.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Before the Third War, this homestead bore a reputation for warmth and hospitality, supporting rich harvests in the heart of Lordaeron. When the Plague swept through the kingdom, the entire family and their laborers succumbed, rising again as husks bound to the Scourge. While feral undead still stumble through the ruined fields, Forsaken forces managed to push the mindless dead out of the main farmhouse, reclaiming the structure to serve as a trading post and foothold along the road toward the eastern glades.",["t"]="A Chilled Hearth"}}}}}
t["subzone:coldridge-pass"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,440,29.541.0,31.157.0,39.231.0,41.190.0,33.179.0",["h"]="b80d70",["n"]="Desfiladero de Crestanevada",["s"]="Desfiladero de Crestanevada. El Desfiladero de Crestanevada es un túnel escarpado y cubierto de nieve que atraviesa la cordillera montañosa meridional de Dun Morogh. Sirve como la única ruta terrestre que conecta los apartados campos de entrenamiento del Valle de Crestanevada con el resto del reino, desembocando cerca de la bulliciosa villa de Kharanos. Debido a que unos troggs hostiles han invadido el paso, cualquier viajero que intente cruzarlo debe abrirse camino luchando o emprender una carrera desesperada hacia el otro lado. Para los jóvenes reclutas enanos y los novicios gnomos que dan sus primeros pasos más allá del Valle de Crestanevada, el Desfiladero de Crestanevada es un duro rito de iniciación. Cincelado directamente a través de la roca, este túnel constituye el enlace principal que envía a los aventureros recién instruidos hacia el este, con rumbo al núcleo fronterizo de Kharanos. Lo que otrora fuera un corredor de montaña seguro se ha convertido en un peligroso cuello de botella, infestado de agresivos troggs que han emergido desde oscuros subterráneos para amenazar a cualquier alma que intente viajar entre el resguardado valle y las extensiones más amplias de Dun Morogh.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarven mountaineers and recruits, traversing Coldridge Pass represents your departure from novice training at Anvilmar into active service across Ironforge's lands.",["race:Gnome"]="Exiled gnomes seeking to aid the Alliance must push through this trogg-infested choke point to reach Kharanos and the higher road toward Ironforge."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The pass connects Coldridge Valley in the southwest to the greater region of Dun Morogh, emptying out into the snowy hills just west of the town of Kharanos.",["al"]={"where does coldridge pass go","coldridge pass destination","how to leave coldridge valley"},["q"]="Where does Coldridge Pass lead?"},{["a"]="Troggs have recently surged forth from the deep subterranean cracks beneath Dun Morogh, seizing dark caves and tunnels throughout the region. Coldridge Pass provided them shelter and an easy ambush point against mountain travelers.",["al"]={"why are troggs here","coldridge pass monsters","trogg infestation"},["q"]="Why are there troggs in Coldridge Pass?"},{["a"]="No, it is not safe. The tunnel is swarming with hostile troggs, meaning recruits and travelers must cut their way through the brutes or sprint through the darkness to reach the opposite end.",["al"]={"is coldridge pass dangerous","can i walk through coldridge pass"},["q"]="Is Coldridge Pass safe to travel through?"},{["a"]="Mountaineers watch the valley and road exits, but the tunnel interior remains contested and uncleared, leaving individual travelers to defend themselves as they make the crossing.",["al"]={"dwarf guards at coldridge pass","who controls the pass"},["q"]="Who guards or maintains the pass?"}},["kw"]={"anvilmar","coldridge pass","coldridge valley","dun morogh","kharanos","mountain pass","trogg","tunnel"},["n"]="Coldridge Pass",["s"]="Coldridge Pass is a rugged, snowbound tunnel cutting through the southern mountain ridge of Dun Morogh. It serves as the sole overland route connecting the secluded training grounds of Coldridge Valley to the rest of the kingdom, emerging near the bustling town of Kharanos. Because hostile troggs have overrun the passage, any traveler attempting the journey must either fight their way through or make a desperate dash for the other side.",["sec"]={{["b"]="For young dwarven recruits and gnome novices taking their first steps beyond Coldridge Valley, Coldridge Pass is a harsh rite of passage. Chiseled straight through the rock, this tunnel forms the primary link sending newly trained adventurers eastward toward the frontier hub of Kharanos. What was once a secure mountain corridor has become a perilous choke point, infested with aggressive troggs that have pushed up from dark sub-terrains to menace any soul trying to travel between the sheltered valley and the wider reaches of Dun Morogh.",["t"]="The Gateway Out of the Valley"}}}}}
t["subzone:coldridge-valley"] = {["faq"]={{["a"]="La única ruta terrestre para salir del valle discurre por el Desfiladero de Crestanevada, un túnel nevado que atraviesa la cordillera hacia el noreste. Una vez cruzado el desfiladero, el camino se dirige hacia el este, directo a la ciudad de Kharanos y en adelante hacia las grandes Puertas de Forjaz.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="8d0d22",["i"]=1,["q"]="",["sp"]=0},{["a"]="Tras la trágica caída de Gnomeregan a manos de los troggs y la lluvia radiactiva, los gnomos supervivientes huyeron a Dun Morogh como refugiados. La gente del Manitas Mayor Mekkatorque fue acogida por el Rey Magni Barbabronce, lo que llevó a muchos aprendices gnomos exiliados a entrenar codo con codo con jóvenes enanos en Yunquemar.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="f6d572",["i"]=2,["q"]="",["sp"]=0},{["a"]="El valle se enfrenta a dos amenazas principales: los hostiles trols Peloescarcha, que resienten los asentamientos enanos en su territorio montañoso, y los toscos troggs Quijaroca, que han surgido de las entrañas de la tierra para bloquear el Desfiladero de Crestanevada. Los depredadores locales, como lobos y jabalíes, también hostigan a los viajeros desprevenidos.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="e29d20",["i"]=3,["q"]="",["sp"]=0},{["a"]="Yunquemar es el pabellón fortaleza central y asentamiento del Valle de Crestanevada. Alberga a instructores de clase, maestros de forja y oficiales montaraces locales que coordinan la defensa del valle y preparan a los aventureros recién instruidos para adentrarse en el resto del mundo.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="60ad03",["i"]=4,["q"]="",["sp"]=0}},["fp"]="16,350,25.508.0,16.522.0,34.256.0,47.293.0,38.283.0,17.249.0",["h"]="203075",["n"]="Valle de Crestanevada",["s"]="Valle de Crestanevada. El Valle de Crestanevada es un valle resguardado y cubierto de nieve, situado en las alturas del suroeste de Dun Morogh. Articulado alrededor de la aldea de Yunquemar, sirve como campo de entrenamiento donde jóvenes enanos y gnomos refugiados toman las armas por primera vez al servicio de Forjaz. Un único túnel, el Desfiladero de Crestanevada, conecta esta hondonada aislada con el resto del reino montañoso. Cobijado por escarpados riscos montañosos, el Valle de Crestanevada permanece prácticamente aislado de las concurridas rutas comerciales de Dun Morogh. En su corazón se encuentra Yunquemar, un robusto salón de piedra y aldea donde veteranos instructores enanos y eruditos gnomos desplazados entrenan a los nuevos reclutas en las artes del combate, el sigilo y la hechicería. Fuera de la calidez de los hogares de Yunquemar, el suelo del valle está cubierto de una espesa capa de nieve y acechado por jabalíes y hambrientos lobos invernales, lo que brinda a los novatos su primera toma de contacto real con la supervivencia en la frontera.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["race:Dwarf"]="As the traditional starting ground for Bronzebeard mountaineers and clerics, the valley represents a dwarf's first steps beyond the hearth and into service of the High Seat.",["race:Gnome"]="For gnome exiles forced from Gnomeregan, the snows of Coldridge Valley offer a safe haven to master their spells and machinery alongside their dwarven hosts."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The only overland route out of the valley leads through Coldridge Pass, a snowy tunnel cutting northeast through the mountain ridge. Once through the pass, the road heads east directly toward the town of Kharanos and onward to the great gates of Ironforge.",["al"]={"exit coldridge","how to get out","path to kharanos"},["q"]="How do you leave Coldridge Valley?"},{["a"]="Following the tragic fall of Gnomeregan to troggs and radioactive fallout, surviving gnomes fled into Dun Morogh as refugees. High Tinker Mekkatorque's people were welcomed by King Magni Bronzebeard, leading many exiled gnomish apprentices to train side by side with young dwarves in Anvilmar.",["al"]={"gnomes in coldridge","why are gnomes here","gnome starting area"},["q"]="Why are gnomes starting here alongside dwarves?"},{["a"]="The valley faces two major menaces: the hostile Frostmane trolls, who resent dwarven settlements on their mountain territory, and crude Rockjaw troggs, who have clawed up from the deep earth to choke Coldridge Pass. Local predators like wolves and boars also harass unwary travelers.",["al"]={"coldridge enemies","valley threats","who is attacking"},["q"]="What threats are troubling the valley?"},{["a"]="Anvilmar is the central fortress-lodge and settlement within Coldridge Valley. It houses class trainers, forge-masters, and local mountaineer officers who coordinate the defense of the valley and prepare newly forged adventurers for the wider world.",["al"]={"anvilmar town","what is the town here"},["q"]="What is Anvilmar?"}},["kw"]={"anvilmar","coldridge pass","coldridge valley","dun morogh","frostmane","ironforge","starting area","troggs"},["n"]="Coldridge Valley",["s"]="Coldridge Valley is a sheltered, snow-covered vale tucked into the southwestern heights of Dun Morogh. Centered around the hamlet of Anvilmar, it serves as the training ground where young dwarves and gnome refugees first take up arms in service of Ironforge. A single tunnel, Coldridge Pass, connects this secluded hollow to the wider mountain realm.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Cradled by sheer mountain cliffs, Coldridge Valley remains largely cut off from the bustling trade routes of Dun Morogh. At its heart sits Anvilmar, a sturdy stone hall and hamlet where veteran dwarven instructors and displaced gnome scholars train fresh recruits in the arts of battle, stealth, and sorcery. Outside the warmth of Anvilmar's hearths, the valley floor is carpeted in thick snow and prowled by boars and hungry winter wolves, providing novices with their first real taste of frontier survival.",["t"]="A Secluded Proving Ground"},{["b"]="Despite its isolation, Coldridge Valley faces immediate danger from two relentless enemies. Indigenous Frostmane trolls have established camps like the Frostmane Hovel, skirmishing with mountaineers and defending their ancestral claims against dwarven encroachment. Worse still, savage Rockjaw troggs have overrun Coldridge Pass, the natural tunnel linking the valley to Kharanos. Until these subterranean brutes are pushed back, travelers and supplies cannot freely move between the valley and the high seat of Ironforge.",["t"]="Encroaching Foes"}}}}}
t["subzone:command-center"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,366,22.537.0,22.335.0,35.248.0,57.166.0,28.168.0,36.134.0",["h"]="bf1c3e",["n"]="Centro de Mando",["s"]="Centro de Mando. El Centro de Mando, a menudo conocido como el Cuartel de Ventormenta, se alza en el corazón del Casco Antiguo como el cuartel general operativo de los oficiales militares de la ciudad. En tiempos de paz alberga al ejército permanente, pero con las fuerzas de Ventormenta desplegadas en fronteras distantes, actualmente opera con una dotación mínima de veteranos centrada en instruir a los reclutas y a la milicia local. Situado en las desgastadas calles del Casco Antiguo, el Centro de Mando sirve como la guarnición principal y el campo de entrenamiento marcial para el reino de Ventormenta. Aunque normalmente está repleto de infantería regular y oficiales de alto rango, las instalaciones se encuentran inusualmente vacías. Con gran parte del ejército real comprometido en campañas en el extranjero, el cuartel depende de un cuadro de instructores veteranos —incluidos Ander Germaine y el artista marcial Wu Shen— para adiestrar a los nuevos guerreros, mientras figuras como Wulf Hansreim entrenan a tiradores para reforzar las defensas de la ciudad.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Hunter"]="Marksmen visiting Stormwind report to the Command Center to learn techniques from veteran trainers such as Wulf Hansreim.",["class:Warrior"]="The Command Center is the primary hub in Stormwind for warrior training, where veterans like Ander Germaine and Wu Shen hone recruits into disciplined frontline soldiers."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Most of Stormwind's standing army has been deployed to distant outposts and foreign battlefields across the world. The Command Center currently maintains only a skeleton crew of seasoned veterans to instruct new recruits and organize local defense.",["al"]={"why few guards here","where is stormwind army","barracks empty"},["q"]="Why is the Command Center so empty?"},{["a"]="Yes. While officially designated the Command Center, city guards and local residents routinely refer to the building as the Stormwind Barracks when giving directions.",["al"]={"stormwind barracks","are command center and barracks the same","barracks location"},["q"]="Is the Command Center the same as the Stormwind Barracks?"},{["a"]="Ander Germaine coordinates and trains the city's warriors alongside instructors like Wu Shen and Ilsa Corbin, while Wulf Hansreim oversees hunter and marksman training.",["al"]={"who trains warriors here","warrior trainer command center","who runs the barracks"},["q"]="Who leads the training here?"},{["a"]="The Command Center is located in Old Town, situated near the Pig and Whistle Tavern and central to the district's training facilities.",["al"]={"where is command center","command center location","how to find command center"},["q"]="Where is the Command Center located?"}},["kw"]={"ander germaine","barracks","command center","hunter trainer","old town","stormwind barracks","warrior trainer","wu shen","wulf hansreim"},["n"]="Command Center",["s"]="The Command Center, often referred to as the Stormwind Barracks, stands in the heart of Old Town as the operational headquarters for the city's military officers. In peacetime, it houses the standing army, but with Stormwind's forces dispatched to distant frontiers, it currently operates with a seasoned skeleton crew focused on drilling recruits and local militia.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Situated within the weathered streets of Old Town, the Command Center serves as the primary garrison and martial training ground for the kingdom of Stormwind. Normally packed with regular infantry and ranking officers, the facility is uncharacteristically sparse. With much of the royal army committed to campaigns abroad, the barracks relies on a veteran cadre of instructors—including Ander Germaine and martial artist Wu Shen—to train fresh warriors, while figures like Wulf Hansreim drill marksmen to bolster the city's defenses.",["t"]="A Thin Line of Defense"},{["b"]="Guards throughout Stormwind often direct newcomers to the 'Barracks' when seeking instruction in heavy arms and tactical combat. The building's proximity to both the Pig and Whistle Tavern and the shadowy operations elsewhere in Old Town makes it an essential anchor of order in a district known for tavern brawls and roguish activity.",["t"]="Old Town's Martial Hub"}}}}}
t["subzone:commons"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="7,278,34.513.0,29.428.0,62.262.0,28.230.0,43.195.0,25.146.0",["h"]="7d9b46",["n"]="Distrito Comercial",["s"]="Distrito Comercial. El Distrito Comercial sirve como el vibrante corazón comercial de Forjaz, conectando la entrada de la ciudad directamente con sus vastas cavernas. Rebosante de mercaderes, viajeros y banqueros, es la vía más transitada de la capital enana y el mercado central de toda la Alianza. Ubicado justo al noreste de las Puertas de Forjaz, el Distrito Comercial es el primer distrito que recibe a los viajeros que entran al reino de la montaña. Esculpida directamente en la piedra, esta bulliciosa calle comercial alberga la principal Casa de Subastas de la Alianza, la Taberna Fuego de Piedra y el banco central de la ciudad dentro de la Cámara Acorazada de Forjaz. Sus amplias avenidas la conectan a la perfección con la Gran Fundición, la Sala Mística y la Sala Militar, garantizando que casi todo el tránsito a pie de la montaña pase por sus concurridos escaparates.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="The Commons acts as the de facto trading floor of the Alliance, drawing heroes from Teldrassil, Stormwind, and Gnomeregan to auction valuable spoils and stock up on supplies.",["race:Dwarf"]="To the Bronzebeard dwarves, the Commons is a source of pride, proving that dwarven hospitality, industry, and commerce can thrive deep within a frozen mountain."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Commons hosts the Alliance's primary Auction House, the city's main bank in the Vault of Ironforge, and the bustling Stonefire Tavern. Its position directly inside the main gates makes it the most convenient gathering and trading place in the entire kingdom.",["al"]={"why is commons busy","why so many players here","ironforge trade hub"},["q"]="What makes the Commons so crowded compared to other districts?"},{["a"]="The Commons connects to almost every major district in Ironforge. Heading southwest leads back to the city gates, northeast connects to the Great Forge, east branches toward the Military Ward, and north leads into the Mystic Ward.",["al"]={"commons exits","how to leave commons","commons directions"},["q"]="Where does the Commons lead?"},{["a"]="Beyond the Auction House and the bank, the Commons features the Ironforge Visitor's Center, Steelfury's Weapon Emporium, the Ironforge Armory, Barim's Reagents, and Fizzlespinner's General Goods.",["al"]={"commons vendors","services in commons","ironforge commons amenities"},["q"]="What key shops and services are found here?"},{["a"]="Yes, the Vault of Ironforge stands prominently along the western wall of the Commons, serving as the city's primary depository and banking center.",["al"]={"where is ironforge bank","ironforge vault","bank location"},["q"]="Is the bank located here?"}},["kw"]={"auction house","bank","commons","ironforge","market","stonefire tavern","vault of ironforge"},["n"]="Commons",["s"]="The Commons serves as the vibrant commercial heart of Ironforge, connecting the city entrance directly to its vast caverns. Teeming with merchants, travelers, and bankers, it is the busiest thoroughfare in the dwarven capital and the central marketplace for the entire Alliance.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Located just northeast of the Gates of Ironforge, the Commons is the first district that greets travelers entering the mountain kingdom. Carved directly out of the stone, this bustling market street houses the primary Alliance Auction House, the Stonefire Tavern, and the city's central bank within the Vault of Ironforge. Broad avenues connect it seamlessly to the Great Forge, the Mystic Ward, and the Military Ward, ensuring that nearly all foot traffic in the mountain passes through its bustling storefronts.",["t"]="The Commercial Hub of the Mountain"},{["b"]="Due to Ironforge's central location on the Eastern Kingdoms continent and its direct underground Deeprun Tram link to Stormwind, the Commons functions as the Alliance's primary trade nexus. Adventurers converge here to trade goods brought from every corner of Azeroth, purchase armaments from merchants like Steelfury and Barim, or meet under the warm lantern light of the local inn before heading out into the Khaz Modan snows.",["t"]="A Crossroads for the Alliance"}}}}}
t["subzone:craftsmen-s-terrace"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="19,341,30.508.0,31.454.0,51.235.0,58.239.0,41.160.0,53.199.0",["h"]="aa227e",["n"]="Bancal del Artesano",["s"]="Bancal del Artesano. El Bancal del Artesano es el bullicioso distrito artesanal situado en los confines septentrionales de Darnassus. Funciona como el principal centro comercial y manufacturero de la capital de los elfos de la noche, albergando talleres, instructores de profesión y una concurrida posada. El distrito también acoge a representantes externos, incluida una embajada de la facción neutral del Alba Argenta. Extendiéndose por el extremo norte de la ciudad de copas arbóreas, el Bancal del Artesano reúne los diversos oficios que mantienen en funcionamiento a Darnassus. Tallistas de madera, peleteros, alquimistas y otros artesanos gestionan aquí sus talleres, combinando los métodos tradicionales de los elfos de la noche con la artesanía práctica. El distrito también ofrece servicios comunitarios esenciales, como una posada, un maestro de hermandad y vendedores de peticiones de hermandad. Sendos puentes conectan el bancal directamente con el Enclave Cenarion al oeste y con el Bancal del Guerrero al sur.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance visitors find the terrace to be one of Darnassus's most welcoming quarters, offering familiar trade supplies, guild administration, and lodging alongside foreign representatives.",["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei, the terrace is proof of their society's self-reliance on Teldrassil, blending ancient craftsmanship with the day-to-day needs of their new capital."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The district houses most of the city's trade profession trainers, craft supply merchants, an inn, and guild registry services. It serves as the commercial center for travelers looking to learn or practice practical skills in Darnassus.",["al"]={"craftsmen services","what is in craftsmens terrace","darnassus trainers"},["q"]="What services are found in the Craftsmen's Terrace?"},{["a"]="The Argent Dawn maintains an embassy in the district to liaise with the night elves and recruit aid against the Scourge. Their presence offers a diplomatic bridge between the Alliance forces in the west and the war-torn lands of Lordaeron.",["al"]={"argent dawn darnassus","argent dawn embassy","why argent dawn here"},["q"]="Why is the Argent Dawn present in the Craftsmen's Terrace?"},{["a"]="The terrace occupies the northern section of Darnassus. You can reach it via bridges leading north from the Warrior's Terrace or east from the Cenarion Enclave.",["al"]={"how to get to craftsmen terrace","craftsmen terrace location","finding craftsmen terrace"},["q"]="How do you reach the Craftsmen's Terrace?"},{["a"]="Scholarly volumes rest throughout the workshops, including histories of the War of the Ancients, the aftermath of the Second War, and a study on the Old Gods housed within the Argent Dawn's quarters.",["al"]={"craftsmen terrace books","lore books darnassus","books in craftsmens terrace"},["q"]="What notable books can be found around the workshops?"}},["kw"]={"argent dawn","artisans","craftsmen's terrace","craftsmens terrace","darnassus","teldrassil","trainers"},["n"]="Craftsmen's Terrace",["s"]="The Craftsmen's Terrace is the bustling artisan district situated in the northern reaches of Darnassus. It serves as the primary trade and manufacturing hub for the night elf capital, housing workshops, profession trainers, and a lively inn. The district also hosts external representatives, including an embassy for the neutral Argent Dawn.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Spanning the northern edge of the canopy city, the Craftsmen's Terrace gathers the diverse trades that keep Darnassus running. Woodworkers, leathercrafters, alchemists, and other artisans operate their shops here, integrating classic night elven methods with practical craft. The district also provides essential community amenities, including an inn, a guild master, and guild petition vendors. Bridges connect the terrace directly to the Cenarion Enclave to the west and the Warrior's Terrace to the south.",["t"]="The Artisan Heart of Darnassus"},{["b"]="Despite the kaldorei's historic isolation, the Craftsmen's Terrace is home to foreign connections, most notably an embassy established by the Argent Dawn to coordinate with northern allies against the Scourge. Visitors browsing the district's various workshops might also stumble across scattered scholarly volumes, ranging from historical accounts of the War of the Ancients to chronicles detailing the Second War and esoteric treatises on the Old Gods.",["t"]="Outside Ties and Forgotten Lore"}}}}}
t["subzone:crag-of-the-everliving"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="22,298,18.491.0,20.427.0,34.261.0,38.196.0,64.170.0,47.219.0",["h"]="db7dfe",["n"]="Risco del Eterno",["s"]="Risco del Eterno. El Risco del Eterno es una cámara cavernosa cubierta de vegetación enclavada en las profundidades de las Cuevas de los Lamentos. Dominada por una flora exuberante y corrupta junto a criaturas vegetales depredadoras, sirve como dominio del Noble del Colmillo Lord Pythas. Sus imponentes niveles superiores albergan a la entidad ancestral que da nombre al risco. Mientras que gran parte de las Cuevas de los Lamentos está excavada en piedra subterránea húmeda, el Risco del Eterno rebosa de una vegetación desmedida y retorcida alimentada por la Pesadilla que corrompe el letargo de Naralex. Imponentes plataformas musgosas y sinuosos senderos están abarrotados de arrastrapiés descarriados: moles vegetales vivientes que merodean por la maleza. Lord Pythas, uno de los discípulos caídos de Naralex, vigila los tramos centrales del risco, habiendo cambiado sus nobles votos druídicos por los ritos venenosos de los Druidas del Colmillo.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="Seeing the Crag of the Everliving is a tragic lesson for Cenarion druids, as pure natural vitality and elemental guardianship have been warped into lethal tools of the Nightmare.",["profession:Herbalism"]="The crag's unnaturally lush subterranean atmosphere nourishes rare underground roots and mushrooms that flourish in the humid, dream-soaked soil."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The chamber is named after Verdan the Everliving, an ancient and colossal plant beast residing in the highest terraces of the crag. Though once an embodiment of nature's timeless vitality, he has fallen under the sway of the Nightmare that afflicts the caverns.",["al"]={"why crag of the everliving","everliving name origin","crag name"},["q"]="Where does this area get its name?"},{["a"]="Lord Pythas, one of the primary Fanglords, directly presides over the crag. In the higher ledges above him lurk both Verdan the Everliving and Lord Serpentis, the leader of the Druids of the Fang.",["al"]={"who is in charge here","crag boss","fanglord here"},["q"]="Who controls this part of the caverns?"},{["a"]="The crag is overrun with Deviate Shamblers—shambling plant horrors birthed from the corrupted springs—alongside twisted serpents and the fanatical Druids of the Fang.",["al"]={"monsters in crag","crag enemies","what lives here"},["q"]="What creatures are commonly found in the Crag of the Everliving?"},{["a"]="The underground springs were harnessed by the night elf druid Naralex to rejuvenate the Barrens. When his ritual was snared by the Emerald Nightmare, the wild growth ran rampant and twisted into hostile, aberrant flora.",["al"]={"why are there plants underground","why so green","corrupted greenery"},["q"]="Why is plant life thriving so deep underground?"}},["kw"]={"barrens","crag of the everliving","deviate shamblers","druids of the fang","lord pythas","lord serpentis","verdan","wailing caverns"},["n"]="Crag of the Everliving",["s"]="The Crag of the Everliving is a verdant cavern chamber nestled deep within the Wailing Caverns. Dominated by lush, corrupted flora and predatory plant creatures, it serves as the domain of the Fanglord Lord Pythas. Its towering upper reaches shelter the ancient entity after whom the crag is named.",["sec"]={{["b"]="While much of the Wailing Caverns is carved of damp subterranean stone, the Crag of the Everliving bursts with unruly, twisted vegetation fueled by the Nightmare corrupting Naralex's slumber. Towering mossy platforms and winding paths are choked with Deviate Shamblers—living plant hulks prowling the undergrowth. Lord Pythas, one of Naralex's fallen disciples, watches over the crag's central reaches, having traded his noble druidic vows for the venomous rites of the Druids of the Fang.",["t"]="A Corrupted Canopy"},{["b"]="The chamber draws its name from Verdan the Everliving, a colossal, primordial plant elemental who resides in the crag's upper heights. Corrupted by the Emerald Nightmare that grips the cavern, Verdan now acts as a fearsome line of defense rather than a peaceful natural guardian. Beyond his towering form lurks Lord Serpentis, the self-proclaimed chief of the Fanglords, who oversees the sect's descent into serpentine madness.",["t"]="The Ancient Guardian"}}}}}
t["subzone:crossroads"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="10,336,32.539.0,28.538.0,48.251.0,48.198.0,58.253.0,46.184.0",["h"]="bbd602",["n"]="El Cruce",["s"]="El Cruce. El Cruce es el corazón del transporte de la Horda por el centro de Kalimdor, situado donde el Camino del Oro de norte a sur se cruza con la ruta que va desde Trinquete hasta Sierra Espolón. Sirve como un bullicioso puesto comercial, zona de preparación militar y centro de tránsito para los viajeros que se desplazan entre Durotar, Mulgore y los frentes del norte. Fiel a su nombre, El Cruce se asienta justo en la intersección del Camino del Oro y la ruta de este a oeste que cruza desde el puerto goblin de Trinquete hasta Sierra Espolón. A pesar de contar con alojamientos modestos, el puesto funciona como un bullicioso centro neurálgico regional. Maestros de jinetes del viento, comerciantes, herreros e instructores mantienen puestos permanentes bajo sus torres de vigilancia. Para los jóvenes guerreros que viajan desde Durotar o Mulgore, el asentamiento suele ser el primer lugar donde son testigos de la vasta logística en múltiples frentes que une a la nueva Horda.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Striking the Crossroads directly cuts off the flow of Horde reinforcements moving between Orgrimmar, Mulgore, and the disputed borders of Ashenvale.",["faction:Horde"]="The Crossroads is the central proving ground and crossroads of your fledgling nation, linking the homelands of the orcs, tauren, and trolls while coordinating supplies across Kalimdor."},["faq"]={{["a"]="It anchors the major transit arteries of central Kalimdor. Every traveler moving overland between Durotar, Mulgore, Ratchet, Stonetalon, or Ashenvale must pass through or near the Crossroads, making it the primary hub for logistics and reinforcements.",["al"]={"why is crossroads important","crossroads purpose","why crossroads matters"},["q"]="Why is the Crossroads so important to the Horde?"},{["a"]="Devrak serves as the flight master at the Crossroads, managing the settlement's wind rider roost and connecting travelers directly to outposts across Kalimdor, including Orgrimmar and Thunder Bluff.",["al"]={"crossroads flight master","who has wyverns here","flight master crossroads"},["q"]="Who provides flight transport at the Crossroads?"},{["a"]="Because the Crossroads is central to Horde transit and located within easy striking distance of both Ashenvale to the north and the neutral port of Ratchet to the east, Alliance raiding parties regularly target the outpost to disrupt Horde supply lines.",["al"]={"why alliance raids crossroads","alliance pvp crossroads","crossroads attacks"},["q"]="Why does the Alliance attack the Crossroads so frequently?"},{["a"]="Barrens raptors raided the Crossroads guard tower and made off with a shipment of silver intended to pay the settlement's defending guards, scattering it into the surrounding savannah.",["al"]={"stolen payroll crossroads","who took the silver","crossroads silver stolen"},["q"]="What happened to the outpost's payroll silver?"}},["kw"]={"barrens","crossroads","devrak","gold road","raptors","ratchet","stonetalon","wind rider"},["n"]="Crossroads",["s"]="The Crossroads is the beating heart of Horde travel through central Kalimdor, situated where the north-south Gold Road intersects the path from Ratchet to the Stonetalon Mountains. It serves as a bustling trading outpost, military staging area, and transit hub for travelers journeying between Durotar, Mulgore, and northern frontlines.",["sec"]={{["b"]="True to its name, the Crossroads sits squarely at the crossing of the Gold Road and the east-west route cutting from the goblin port of Ratchet into the Stonetalon Mountains. Despite having modest lodgings, the outpost functions as a bustling regional hub. Wind rider masters, merchants, blacksmiths, and trainers maintain permanent setups beneath its watchtowers. For young warriors traveling out from Durotar or Mulgore, the settlement is often the first place they witness the vast, multi-front logistics binding the new Horde together.",["t"]="A Vital Junction in the Savannah"},{["b"]="Maintaining order at the Crossroads is a relentless struggle. Local wildlife—including plains raptors bold enough to plunder payroll silver from the guard towers—poses a persistent nuisance, while harpies, quilboar, and centaur tribes continually pressure the perimeter. Beyond the threats native to the Barrens, the settlement's proximity to neutral Ratchet and the contested forests of Ashenvale makes it a prime target for encroaching Alliance scouting parties, leading to frequent skirmishes just outside its defensive barricades.",["t"]="Frontier Outpost Under Siege"}}}}}
t["subzone:crusader-outpost"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,340,18.492.0,31.433.0,29.184.0,26.156.0,41.232.0,31.150.0",["h"]="09704a",["n"]="Avanzada de los Cruzados",["s"]="Avanzada de los Cruzados. La Avanzada de los Cruzados es una torre de vigilancia fortificada situada en lo alto de las escarpadas colinas del este de los Claros de Tirisfal. Guarnecida por celosos miembros de la Cruzada Escarlata, vigila los accesos que conducen hacia su bastión en el Monasterio Escarlata. Desde esta altura, los cruzados observan el tránsito por el camino y están preparados para repeler cualquier incursión de los Renegados. Construida en los riscos que dominan el camino oriental, la Avanzada de los Cruzados sirve como principal estación de alerta temprana para la Cruzada Escarlata. Desde su elevada torre, los centinelas vigilan el movimiento entre Rémol y los confines orientales de Lordaeron, asegurándose de que los no-muertos errantes o los grupos de exploración sean avistados mucho antes de alcanzar las puertas del Monasterio. La torre también otorga a la guarnición la capacidad táctica de flanquear a cualquier fuerza que intente marchar valle arriba hacia su sagrado bastión.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="Navigating the eastern trails of Tirisfal requires caution, as Scarlet sentries atop this hill will swiftly attack anyone traveling toward the Monastery.",["race:Undead"]="This watchtower sits right on the edge of Forsaken territory, serving as a bitter reminder that zealous living crusaders still hold sovereign pockets within the glades."},["faq"]={{["a"]="It is a fortified scouting tower held by the Scarlet Crusade in eastern Tirisfal Glades. It monitors the road passing below and protects the southern approach to the Scarlet Monastery.",["al"]={"what is this tower","crusader outpost tirisfal","scarlet watchtower"},["q"]="What is the Crusader Outpost?"},{["a"]="The outpost is manned by zealots of the Scarlet Crusade under the command of Captain Vachon. They view all undead as abominations to be eradicated on sight.",["al"]={"who owns crusader outpost","who lives here","scarlet crusade outpost"},["q"]="Who controls this outpost?"},{["a"]="Its elevated position offers clear sightlines over the main eastern thoroughfare of Tirisfal Glades. This allows Crusaders to detect Forsaken troop movements early and flank any forces attempting an assault on the Scarlet Monastery.",["al"]={"why build here","outpost location","tactical purpose"},["q"]="Why is the tower situated in these hills?"},{["a"]="Yes. The Scarlet Crusade considers all outsiders—particularly the Forsaken and their Horde allies—corrupt enemies who must be purged in holy fire.",["al"]={"is crusader outpost hostile","are they aggressive"},["q"]="Will the guards here attack me?"}},["kw"]={"captain vachon","crusader outpost","scarlet crusade","scarlet monastery","scout tower","tirisfal glades","watchtower"},["n"]="Crusader Outpost",["s"]="Crusader Outpost is a fortified watchtower perched atop the rugged hills of eastern Tirisfal Glades. Manned by zealous members of the Scarlet Crusade, it guards the approaches leading toward their stronghold at the Scarlet Monastery. From this height, Crusaders observe travel along the road and stand ready to repel any Forsaken incursion.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Built into the bluffs overlooking the eastern road, the Crusader Outpost serves as a primary early-warning station for the Scarlet Crusade. From their elevated tower, sentries watch over movement between Brill and the eastern reaches of Lordaeron, ensuring that wandering undead or scouting parties are spotted long before reaching the Monastery gates. The tower also grants the garrison tactical flanking capability against any force seeking to march up the valley toward their holy bastion.",["t"]="Eyes Over Tirisfal"},{["b"]="Under the command of Scarlet officers like Captain Vachon, the garrison stationed here maintains unwavering vigilance. They see the surrounding woods not as sovereign territory of the Forsaken, but as unhallowed soil stolen from humanity by monstrosities. For travelers loyal to the Undercity, the outpost represents an ever-present ambush point where crossbow bolts and cleansing steel await anyone straying too close to the bluffs.",["t"]="A Thorn in the Dark Lady's Side"}}}}}
t["subzone:crystal-lake"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="12,248,16.478.0,17.352.0,30.154.0,41.227.0,41.198.0,43.203.0",["h"]="7e06ed",["n"]="Lago de Cristal",["s"]="Lago de Cristal. El Lago de Cristal es una masa de agua situada justo al este de Villadorada, en el corazón del Bosque de Elwynn. Aunque antaño era un lugar tranquilo, sus costas han sido invadidas por agresivos múrlocs, convirtiéndose en un peligro habitual para los lugareños y los viajeros de paso. Situado a poca distancia a pie de la Posada Orgullo de León, el Lago de Cristal debería ser un idílico retiro rural, pero está plagado de fauna peligrosa. Tribus de múrlocs de agua dulce se han apoderado de la orilla y de los bajíos, atacando a cualquiera que se acerque demasiado. El alquimista local William Mortero contrata con frecuencia a los aventureros que pasan por allí para que se aventuren hasta la orilla del agua, indicándoles que derroten a las criaturas y recolecten las algas de cristal que portan para utilizarlas en sus brebajes experimentales.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="The murloc infestation so close to Goldshire underscores how thinly stretched the kingdom's military has become in safeguarding its core territories.",["profession:Herbalism"]="The freshwater shallows harbor Crystal Kelp, though it is primarily gathered directly from the resident murlocs who harvest it from the lake bed."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Crystal Lake lies directly east of the crossroads town of Goldshire in central Elwynn Forest, easily reached by walking past the outskirts of the village.",["al"]={"crystal lake location","where is crystal lake","find crystal lake"},["q"]="Where is Crystal Lake located?"},{["a"]="Like many waterways in Elwynn Forest, Crystal Lake provides a natural freshwater habitat where murlocs can nest and forage. Their numbers have swelled close to Goldshire due to the strained resources of Stormwind's local guard.",["al"]={"why murlocs crystal lake","murloc problem goldshire","crystal lake murlocs"},["q"]="Why are murlocs gathered at Crystal Lake?"},{["a"]="The grave marker on the central island reads only 'Deeply missed, never forgotten.' There is no name etched upon the stone, leaving the identity of the person buried there an enduring local mystery.",["al"]={"crystal lake grave","tombstone on island elwynn","who is buried at crystal lake"},["q"]="Whose grave is on the island in the lake?"},{["a"]="William Pestle, an apothecary working out of Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, contracts adventurers to slay the murlocs along the shore to gather crystal kelp, which he requires for an invisibility potion.",["al"]={"william pestle crystal lake","kelp quest crystal lake","invisibility potion elwynn"},["q"]="What do adventurers need from Crystal Lake?"}},["kw"]={"crystal kelp","crystal lake","elwynn","goldshire","grave","jason mathers","murloc","william pestle"},["n"]="Crystal Lake",["s"]="Crystal Lake is a body of water lying just east of Goldshire in the heart of Elwynn Forest. While once a peaceful spot, its shores have been overrun by aggressive murlocs, turning it into a frequent hazard for local villagers and passing travelers.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Situated within walking distance of Lion's Pride Inn, Crystal Lake should be an idyllic rural retreat, but it is plagued by dangerous wildlife. Tribes of freshwater murlocs have claimed the shoreline and shallow shoals, attacking anyone who strays too close. Local alchemist William Pestle frequently hires passing adventurers to venture to the water's edge, directing them to defeat the creatures and harvest the crystal kelp they carry for use in his experimental concoctions.",["t"]="A Troubled Shore"},{["b"]="Resting quietly in the center of the lake is a tiny, isolated islet. Solitary and overgrown, it bears a simple grave marked with the tender inscription: 'Deeply missed, never forgotten.' The identity of whoever rests beneath the soil remains unrecorded in town ledgers, providing a somber mystery amidst the surrounding croaks of the shoreline murlocs.",["t"]="The Silent Island"}}}}}
t["subzone:cut-throat-alley"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,287,15.663.0,35.264.0,48.219.0,37.189.0,41.146.0",["h"]="5a1bf5",["n"]="Callejón de los Degolladores",["s"]="Callejón de los Degolladores. Callejón de los Degolladores es un rincón apartado y deshabitado de la Ciudad de Ventormenta, oculto tras las tiendas de los canales. Escondido detrás de un establecimiento llamado La Dama Sombría, cerca del límite con Distrito de los Enanos, consta de un patio tranquilo y una residencia vacía aislada del tránsito habitual de la ciudad. Callejón de los Degolladores es uno de los rincones más silenciosos y reservados de Ventormenta. Aunque técnicamente figura cartografiado junto al Distrito de los Enanos, no comparte en absoluto los rugientes fuegos de las forjas ni el denso hollín de dicho distrito. No se puede acceder al callejón desde ninguna de las avenidas principales de la ciudad; el único paso a pie atraviesa directamente La Dama Sombría, una pequeña tienda situada junto a los canales, justo al sur del puente de la Plaza de la Catedral. Tras la puerta del comercio se halla un pequeño callejón sin salida pavimentado, repleto de cajas apiladas, barriles olvidados y una única residencia desocupada de dos plantas. Completamente oculto a la vista de los guardias que patrullan y de los ciudadanos corrientes, reposa en absoluto silencio en medio del bullicio de la capital.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Rogue"]="Accessible only through the rear door of a shady canal shop, this unpatrolled dead-end offers an ideal hideout for anyone who prefers to stay out of sight of the Stormwind City Guard."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Head to the canal front along the edge of the Dwarven District, just south of the footbridge leading to Cathedral Square. Look for a shop named the Shady Lady. Walking straight through the back of this establishment brings you right out into the tucked-away alley.",["al"]={"find cut throat alley","cut throat alley location","where is cut-throat alley","how to enter cut-throat alley"},["q"]="How do you get to Cut-Throat Alley?"},{["a"]="The outdoor passage shares the broader Dwarven District subzone label on common maps. The name 'Cut-Throat Alley' only reveals itself on your compass once you step inside the empty two-story home at the back of the lot.",["al"]={"minimap dwarven district","why does it say dwarven district","cut-throat alley name bug"},["q"]="Why does the map call this the Dwarven District?"},{["a"]="No. The alley and its lone two-story house are completely abandoned. Aside from stacked cargo crates and empty barrels, there are no residents, shopkeepers, or city watchmen stationed here.",["al"]={"cut throat alley npcs","who lives in cut throat alley","empty house cut throat alley"},["q"]="Is anyone living in Cut-Throat Alley?"},{["a"]="There are no formal duties or civic assignments that lead into the alley. It serves purely as an overlooked, secluded backdrop within the capital.",["al"]={"cut throat alley quests","cut throat alley storyline"},["q"]="Are there any quests in Cut-Throat Alley?"}},["kw"]={"cathedral square","cut-throat alley","dwarven district","secret alley","shady lady","stormwind canals"},["n"]="Cut-Throat Alley",["s"]="Cut-Throat Alley is a secluded, unpopulated back corner of Stormwind City hidden away behind the canal shops. Tucked behind a storefront called the Shady Lady near the Dwarven District border, it consists of a quiet courtyard and an empty residence cut off from normal city foot traffic.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Cut-Throat Alley is one of Stormwind's quietest and most secretive corners. Though technically charted alongside the Dwarven District, it shares none of the district's roaring forge fires or heavy soot. The alley cannot be reached from any of the city's main avenues; the only foot path leads straight through the Shady Lady, a small shop lining the canals just south of the bridge from Cathedral Square. Beyond the shop door lies a small paved dead-end lined with stacked crates, forgotten barrels, and a single unoccupied two-story residence. Completely hidden from passing guards and ordinary citizens, it sits entirely silent amidst the bustle of the capital.",["t"]="A Secluded Nook"}}}}}
t["subzone:dagger-hills"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="12,278,14.431.0,20.444.0,35.130.0,30.151.0,36.172.0,18.160.0",["h"]="89927b",["n"]="Las Colinas Afiladas",["s"]="Las Colinas Afiladas. Las Colinas Afiladas forman una escarpada cresta que se alza a lo largo del sur de Páramos de Poniente, justo detrás del pueblo devastado de Arroyo de la Luna. Desatendidas durante mucho tiempo por la corona, estas tierras altas y rocosas sirven como un refugio hostil para degolladores, bandidos y horrores acechantes que amenazan las llanuras circundantes. Elevándose muy por encima del ruinoso asentamiento de Arroyo de la Luna, Las Colinas Afiladas marcan los escarpados confines meridionales de Páramos de Poniente. Desprovistas de patrullas reales oficiales de Ventormenta, estas áridas tierras altas se han convertido en una fortificación natural para la Hermandad Defias. Pendencieros, acechacampos y salteadores de caminos merodean entre las crestas rocosas y los matorrales, emboscando a los viajeros incautos y vigilando los accesos a sus fortalezas más abajo.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="The hills represent the utter breakdown of law in southern Westfall, where Gryan Stoutmantle's People's Militia must fight to reclaim ground surrendered by Stormwind's absence.",["race:Dwarf"]="The solitary presence of Grimbooze Thunderbrew on this exposed ridge shows the sheer stubbornness of dwarven brewers searching for undisturbed space to perfect their craft."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Dagger Hills form the high, rocky southern border of Westfall, standing directly behind the abandoned settlement of Moonbrook.",["al"]={"dagger hills location","where is dagger hills","how to get to dagger hills"},["q"]="Where are the Dagger Hills located?"},{["a"]="The Defias Brotherhood maintains a heavy presence across the ridge, deploying highwaymen, pathstalkers, and knuckledusters to guard the southern hills.",["al"]={"dagger hills defias","who lives in dagger hills","enemies in dagger hills"},["q"]="Who controls the Dagger Hills?"},{["a"]="Grimbooze Thunderbrew has set up his distilling works in these lonely heights to craft his potent dwarven brews, braving bandits and beasts alike in the name of good drink.",["al"]={"grimbooze westfall","dwarf in dagger hills","grimbooze thunderbrew lore"},["q"]="Why is a dwarf brewing ale out here?"},{["a"]="Leprithus is an infamous ghoul known to roam the crags of the Dagger Hills, terrifying any travelers or bandits unfortunate enough to run across it in the dark.",["al"]={"leprithus spawn","ghoul in dagger hills","dagger hills undead"},["q"]="What is Leprithus?"}},["kw"]={"dagger hills","defias","grimbooze","leprithus","moonbrook","thunderbrew","westfall"},["n"]="Dagger Hills",["s"]="The Dagger Hills form a rugged ridge rising across southern Westfall, directly behind the blighted town of Moonbrook. Long neglected by the crown, this rocky highland serves as a hostile hideout for cutthroats, bandits, and creeping terrors that threaten the surrounding plains.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Rising high above the dilapidated settlement of Moonbrook, the Dagger Hills mark the jagged southern reaches of Westfall. Stripped of official royal patrols from Stormwind, this arid highland has become a natural fortification for the Defias Brotherhood. Knuckledusters, pathstalkers, and highwaymen lurk among the rocky crests and scrub, ambushing unwary travelers and keeping watch over the approaches to their strongholds below.",["t"]="A Bandit Haven"},{["b"]="Beyond mortal outlaws, the Dagger Hills carry an eerie reputation under cover of darkness. The unsettling specter Leprithus, a wandering ghoul, has been sighted stalking the desolate heights when the sun dips. Aside from wandering outlaws and lingering undead, the only resident willing to brave the ridge is Grimbooze Thunderbrew, a dwarven brewer who sets up his distilling equipment in the rugged wilderness regardless of the nearby dangers.",["t"]="Shadows on the Ridge"}}}}}
t["subzone:darkcloud-pinnacle"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="18,273,21.385.0,20.328.1,32.157.0,36.177.0,29.121.0,37.170.0",["h"]="bcf0a9",["n"]="Cumbre de la Nube Negra",["s"]="Cumbre de la Nube Negra. Cumbre de la Nube Negra es un asentamiento tauren fortificado situado sobre varias mesetas interconectadas al este de El Gran Elevador, en Las Mil Agujas. En manos del belicoso clan Tótem Siniestro, esta fortaleza en las alturas sirve como base de operaciones para desestabilizar la región y llevar a cabo turbios negocios. Distribuida a lo largo de tres mesetas principales unidas por puentes de cuerda, Cumbre de la Nube Negra domina la cuenca del cañón que se extiende a sus pies. A las alturas solo se puede acceder mediante una empinada pendiente natural que asciende desde el fondo del cañón cruzando puentes de madera, o a través de un paso elevado cerca de Zahúrda Rajacieno. Desde estas rocas azotadas por el viento, los Tótem Siniestro vigilan el valle, a salvo de asaltos fortuitos y aislados del resto de tribus tauren.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="The Grimtotem occupying this mesa act as hostiles, menacing travelers passing from the Great Lift deeper into Thousand Needles.",["race:Tauren"]="The Grimtotem's treacherous behavior on these mesas stands in stark opposition to the unity and peace Cairne Bloodhoof strives to maintain among the tribes."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The stronghold belongs to the Grimtotem clan, an aggressive and reclusive tauren faction openly hostile to most outsiders and deeply suspicious of the Horde.",["al"]={"who lives at darkcloud pinnacle","darkcloud pinnacle owners","who is at darkcloud pinnacle"},["q"]="Who controls Darkcloud Pinnacle?"},{["a"]="The pinnacle can be accessed by climbing a natural ramp up an adjacent mesa from the canyon floor and crossing wooden rope bridges, or via a bridge situated near Razorfen Downs.",["al"]={"how to get up darkcloud pinnacle","darkcloud pinnacle path","entrance to darkcloud pinnacle"},["q"]="How do you reach Darkcloud Pinnacle?"},{["a"]="The settlement's operations are overseen by prominent Grimtotem figures, including Arnak Grimtotem and Harb Foulmountain.",["al"]={"darkcloud pinnacle leaders","who leads darkcloud pinnacle","grimtotem bosses"},["q"]="Who leads the Grimtotem here?"},{["a"]="The Grimtotem at the pinnacle maintain secret communications with an unknown dark influence, working toward shadowy goals that threaten the stability of Thousand Needles.",["al"]={"what is happening at darkcloud pinnacle","grimtotem conspiracy"},["q"]="What are the Grimtotem plotting here?"}},["kw"]={"arnak grimtotem","darkcloud pinnacle","grimtotem","harb foulmountain","mesa","thousand needles"},["n"]="Darkcloud Pinnacle",["s"]="Darkcloud Pinnacle is a fortified tauren settlement perched atop several interconnected mesas east of the Great Lift in Thousand Needles. Held by the aggressive Grimtotem clan, the aerial stronghold serves as a base of operations for regional disruption and shady dealings.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Spanning three main mesas joined by rope bridges, Darkcloud Pinnacle commands the canyon basin below. The heights are accessible only by a steep natural slope leading from the canyon floor across wooden bridges, or via a high crossing near Razorfen Downs. From these windswept rocks, the Grimtotem watch the valley, safe from casual assault and isolated from the broader tauren tribes.",["t"]="A Clifftop Stronghold"},{["b"]="Commanded by leaders such as Arnak Grimtotem and Harb Foulmountain, the settlement is more than a simple outpost. Secret correspondence discovered on the mesa suggests the Grimtotem are actively coordinating with dark and unknown powers, pursuing ambitions far removed from the peace forged by Cairne Bloodhoof in Thunder Bluff.",["t"]="Schemes on the Mesas"}}}}}
t["subzone:darkshire"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="9,262,16.635.0,20.574.0,43.376.0,45.362.0,20.268.0,24.277.0,24.323.0",["h"]="a2c6cc",["n"]="Villa Oscura",["s"]="Villa Oscura. Villa Oscura, anteriormente conocida como Grand Hamlet, es un maltrecho asentamiento en el este de Bosque del Ocaso. Envuelto en una penumbra antinatural y duradera y desatendido por Ventormenta, el pueblo sobrevive únicamente gracias a la vigilancia de la Guardia Nocturna y a la obstinada resistencia de sus gentes. Antaño un pacífico asentamiento boscoso llamado Grand Hamlet, la aldea fue arrasada por la Antigua Horda durante la Primera Guerra y reconstruida más tarde. Su destino se volvió verdaderamente aciago tras la caída de Medivh en Karazhan, cuyos estertores de muerte maldijeron Brightwood hasta convertirlo en el sombrío páramo que ahora se llama Bosque del Ocaso. A pesar de ser una posesión nominal del Reino de Ventormenta, el ayuntamiento apenas recibe ayuda de la corona. La parálisis política en Ciudad de Ventormenta ha dejado a la guarnición sin efectivos y las fronteras sin patrullar, lo que ha obligado al alcalde Ello Cerranegro y al consejo local a impartir su propia justicia, dura y aislacionista, en las sombras.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Paladin"]="With the dead rising in every surrounding cemetery and the Light all but forgotten by frightened locals, holy warriors find no shortage of unholy blights to purge around the village perimeter.",["faction:Alliance"]="Darkshire is a stark reminder of the kingdom's fracturing frontier. Alliance heroes will find grateful townsfolk, but also palpable bitterness toward the unresponsive nobility back in Stormwind City."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The settlement was originally named Grand Hamlet when the region was still the sunny forest of Brightwood. After the Guardian Medivh died at nearby Karazhan, dark magic crept across the woods, blocking the sunlight and raising the dead. As Brightwood decayed into Duskwood, the bleak reality of their cursed surroundings prompted the residents to rename the village Darkshire.",["al"]={"why is it called darkshire","grand hamlet name change","darkshire history"},["q"]="Why was the town renamed from Grand Hamlet?"},{["a"]="Stormwind is paralyzed by domestic political gridlock following the disappearance of King Varian Wrynn. Under the guidance of royal court advisors like Lady Katrana Prestor, the crown has focused its remaining resources narrowly around Elwynn and Redridge, leaving outlying settlements like Darkshire to fend entirely for themselves without soldiers or supplies.",["al"]={"where is the stormwind army","why no guards in duskwood","why did stormwind abandon darkshire"},["q"]="Why isn't Stormwind helping defend Darkshire?"},{["a"]="Civic authority rests with Lord Ello Ebonlocke and the Council of Darkshire, operating out of the town hall alongside town clerk Daltry. Martial defense is led by Ello's daughter, Commander Althea Ebonlocke, who commands the volunteer militia known as the Night Watch.",["al"]={"who is in charge of darkshire","darkshire leadership","mayor of darkshire"},["q"]="Who leads Darkshire?"},{["a"]="The Night Watch is a local civilian militia formed out of necessity by Althea Ebonlocke. Because the Stormwind Army will not deploy troops to Duskwood, local townsfolk took up arms to patrol the gloomy roads, secure the borders, and push back ghoul incursions and rogue beasts.",["al"]={"what is the nightwatch","darkshire guards","who protects darkshire"},["q"]="What is the Night Watch?"},{["a"]="Morgan Ladimore was a returning veteran of the Third War who arrived in Darkshire only to discover his homestead ruined and his family gone. After a local priest suggested looking among the tombstones at Raven Hill Cemetery, grief and tragedy drove Ladimore to his death, leaving a dark legacy that still haunts the region.",["al"]={"morla dime lore","ladimore darkshire","who is the ladimore guy"},["q"]="Who was Morgan Ladimore?"}},["kw"]={"brightwood","darkshire","duskwood","ebonlocke","grand hamlet","night watch","scarlet raven"},["n"]="Darkshire",["s"]="Darkshire, formerly known as Grand Hamlet, is a battered settlement in eastern Duskwood. Cloaked in an enduring, unnatural gloom and neglected by Stormwind, the town survives only through the vigilance of the Night Watch and the stubborn endurance of its people.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Once a peaceful woodland settlement called Grand Hamlet, the village was razed by the Old Horde during the First War and later rebuilt. Its fortune turned truly bitter following the fall of Medivh at Karazhan, whose lingering death throes cursed Brightwood into the shadowy wilderness now called Duskwood. Despite being a nominal holding of the Kingdom of Stormwind, the town hall receives virtually no aid from the crown. Political paralysis in Stormwind City has left the garrison unstaffed and the borders unpatrolled, forcing Mayor Ello Ebonlocke and the local council to administer their own harsh, insular justice in the shadows.",["t"]="A Town Abandoned"},{["b"]="Surrounded by walking dead from the western graveyards and feral worgen hunting through the woods, Darkshire clings to life along its palisades. The town's primary shield is the Night Watch, a voluntary civilian militia commanded by Althea Ebonlocke. Operating out of the town square and patrolling the pitch-black thoroughfares, these weary sentries keep the town's roads open and turn back the terrors prowling the tree line. Travelers arriving at the Scarlet Raven Tavern find the locals suspicious, frightened, and desperate for any mercenary capable of holding a blade.",["t"]="The Line in the Dark"}}}}}
t["subzone:darkshire-town-hall"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="19,278,21.556.0,38.263.0,43.229.0,57.255.0",["h"]="5301ab",["n"]="ayuntamiento de Villa Oscura",["s"]="ayuntamiento de Villa Oscura. ayuntamiento de Villa Oscura se alza en el extremo occidental de la plaza del pueblo como la sede del gobierno local en el Bosque del Ocaso. Desde el interior de estas salas tenuemente iluminadas, el alcalde Lord Ello Cerranegro y su consejo intentan administrar un asentamiento asediado por una oscuridad insidiosa y monstruosidades no-muertas. Ubicado directamente al oeste de la plaza principal del pueblo, el ayuntamiento es el lugar donde los líderes cívicos de Villa Oscura se reúnen para gobernar un territorio cada vez más aislado. Entre sus muros desgastados se encuentra el alcalde Lord Ello Cerranegro, quien lucha por preservar el orden civil y proteger a la población mientras Ventormenta ofrece muy poca ayuda militar. Junto al alcalde, funcionarios municipales como el dependiente Daltry trabajan para llevar el registro local y seguir la pista de los viajeros que desafían los peligrosos caminos del Bosque del Ocaso, aunque mantener los libros al día es una tarea sombría y difícil en tiempos tan aciagos.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance travelers, the Town Hall represents the fragile authority of the kingdom's southern frontiers, showing how thin Stormwind's protection stretches in isolated settlements."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Lord Ello Ebonlocke serves as the Mayor of Darkshire and presides over the town council from inside the Town Hall. He directs local defenses and appeals to visiting adventurers for help, as the town receives virtually no reinforcements from the kingdom's capital.",["al"]={"who is the mayor","who runs darkshire","who is in the town hall"},["q"]="Who leads the town from this building?"},{["a"]="Clerk Daltry maintains town registries documenting the residents and the travelers passing through Darkshire. Due to the chaos and frequent dangers plaguing Duskwood, many of his logs and records have fallen somewhat out of date.",["al"]={"clerk daltry records","what does daltry do","town registry"},["q"]="What records are kept inside the Town Hall?"},{["a"]="With Duskwood cut off from direct military support from Stormwind, the Town Hall functions as the operational hub for the Night Watch and local authorities. It is where the council coordinates civilian defense and dispatches aid across the shadowy region.",["al"]={"why does the town hall matter","darkshire council role"},["q"]="Why is the Town Hall so important to Duskwood's survival?"}},["kw"]={"clerk daltry","council","darkshire","duskwood","ello ebonlocke","town hall"},["n"]="Darkshire Town Hall",["s"]="Darkshire Town Hall stands on the western edge of the town square as the seat of local governance in Duskwood. From inside these dimly lit halls, Mayor Lord Ello Ebonlocke and his council attempt to administer a settlement besieged by creeping darkness and undead monstrosities.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Located directly west of the main town square, the Town Hall is where Darkshire's civic leadership gathers to govern an increasingly isolated territory. Within its weathered walls sits Mayor Lord Ello Ebonlocke, struggling to preserve civil order and protect the populace while Stormwind offers little in the way of military aid. Alongside the mayor, municipal officials like Clerk Daltry work to track local records and the travelers braving Duskwood's dangerous roads, though keeping ledgers current is a grim and challenging task in such perilous times.",["t"]="The Seat of Darkshire"}}}}}
t["subzone:darkspear-strand"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,286,16.539.0,34.270.0,43.233.0,52.206.0",["h"]="7d9bb8",["n"]="Playa de Lanza Negra",["s"]="Playa de Lanza Negra. Playa de Lanza Negra es el tramo de costa en el sur de Durotar donde los trols de Lanza Negra llegaron a la orilla tras su exilio de las Islas del Eco. Situada justo al lado de Poblado Sen'jin, esta playa marca el amargo comienzo del refugio de la tribu en el continente bajo el liderazgo de Vol'jin. Cuando el médico brujo Zalazane enloqueció y tomó el control de las Islas del Eco, los trols de Lanza Negra supervivientes se vieron obligados a abandonar su hogar insular. Los refugiados, desesperados, cruzaron las estrechas aguas y desembarcaron a lo largo de esta costa blanqueada por el sol. En lugar de dispersarse por los hostiles páramos rojos de Durotar, los supervivientes se unieron a escasos metros tierra adentro desde la costa para construir Poblado Sen'jin. Hoy en día, la playa sirve como un silencioso recordatorio de su desplazamiento, con vistas al oleaje hacia las islas que aún esperan recuperar.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="The strand marks the southern coast where the Darkspear cemented their place on the Kalimdor mainland beside their Orc allies after losing their island settlement.",["race:Troll"]="For Darkspear trolls, stepping onto this shore carries the sting of Zalazane's betrayal and the bittersweet memory of escaping with their lives to found Sen'jin Village."},["faq"]={{["a"]="This coastline is where the Darkspear trolls made landfall after fleeing the Echo Isles. When Zalazane turned his dark magic against his own people, the survivors evacuated across the water and came ashore here, immediately gathering nearby to establish Sen'jin Village.",["al"]={"why is it called darkspear strand","darkspear strand lore","what is this beach"},["q"]="What happened at Darkspear Strand?"},{["a"]="The witch doctor Zalazane betrayed his kin and used dark voodoo to enslave the minds of his fellow tribesfolk. Chief Vol'jin led the remaining uncorrupted Darkspear off the islands to escape total subjugation, landing on this strand.",["al"]={"why did trolls leave echo isles","zalazane exile","echo isles evacuation"},["q"]="Why did the Darkspear leave the Echo Isles?"},{["a"]="Sen'jin Village sits just yards inland from the beach. It was established by the refugees immediately after landing on the strand and serves as the primary Darkspear outpost and spiritual center in Durotar.",["al"]={"village near darkspear strand","town next to beach","sen'jin village location"},["q"]="What settlement is located next to Darkspear Strand?"}},["kw"]={"darkspear","darkspear strand","durotar","echo isles","sen'jin village","vol'jin","zalazane"},["n"]="Darkspear Strand",["s"]="Darkspear Strand is the stretch of coastline in southern Durotar where the Darkspear trolls washed ashore following their exile from the Echo Isles. Located directly beside Sen'jin Village, this beach marks the bitter beginning of the tribe's mainland refuge under Vol'jin's leadership.",["sec"]={{["b"]="When the witch doctor Zalazane went mad and seized control of the Echo Isles, the surviving Darkspear trolls were forced to abandon their offshore home. Desperate refugees crossed the narrow waters and landed along this sun-bleached coast. Rather than scatter into the hostile red wastes of Durotar, the survivors banded together just yards inland from the shoreline to construct Sen'jin Village. Today, the strand serves as a quiet reminder of their displacement, looking out across the surf toward the islands they still hope to reclaim.",["t"]="A Shore of Exile"}}}}}
t["subzone:dawning-isles"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,248,18.460.0,19.353.0,36.149.0,41.250.0,42.205.0",["h"]="d83da5",["n"]="Islas del Alba",["s"]="Islas del Alba. Las Islas del Alba son un grupo de islotes bajos situados en el Lago Lordamere, a lo largo del extremo oriental de Bosque de Argénteos. En su día fueron retiros idílicos, pero han sucumbido al añublo de la Plaga de la No-Muerte y están invadidos por agresivos múrlocs. Antes de la Tercera Guerra, las Islas del Alba eran conocidas como pintorescos cayos que reposaban sobre las aguas tranquilas y cristalinas del Lago Lordamere. Cuando la Plaga de la No-Muerte arrasó Lordaeron, la corrupción se filtró en los bajíos del lago. La vegetación se volvió pálida y putrefacta, desvaneciendo su idílica tranquilidad. Hoy en día, la tribu de múrlocs Vile Fin domina las orillas enfangadas y la maleza enmarañada, defendiendo con agresividad sus florecientes colonias de cualquiera que intente cruzar el lago.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="The blighted islands serve as a grim reminder of how far the corruption of the Scourge reached into Lordaeron's most scenic waters.",["race:Undead"]="The blighted Dawning Isles lie on Lordamere Lake, within sight of the western approaches to the Undercity, and the Vile Fin murlocs that hold them grow more numerous each year."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Dawning Isles are located in Lordamere Lake, bordering the eastern boundary of Silverpine Forest and resting just west of the Ruins of Lordaeron.",["al"]={"dawning isles location","where is dawning isles","dawning islands map"},["q"]="Where are the Dawning Isles located?"},{["a"]="The islands are primarily infested by the Vile Fin tribe of murlocs, which thrives along the corrupted shorelines. In the past, dangerous bog beasts also prowled the islets, though they have largely vanished in favor of the teeming murloc population.",["al"]={"mobs on dawning isles","what lives on dawning isles","dawning isle monsters"},["q"]="What creatures inhabit the Dawning Isles?"},{["a"]="The islands were tainted during the Third War when the Plague of Undeath swept Lordaeron. The water and soil absorbed the blight, poisoning the vegetation and leaving the islets murky, sickly, and decayed.",["al"]={"why are dawning isles blighted","lake blight dawning isles"},["q"]="Why are the trees and shores rotting here?"}},["kw"]={"dawning isles","lordaeron","lordamere lake","silverpine forest","vile fin"},["n"]="Dawning Isles",["s"]="The Dawning Isles are a cluster of low-lying islets situated within Lordamere Lake along the eastern edge of Silverpine Forest. Once idyllic retreats, they have succumbed to the blight of the Plague of Undeath and are overrun by aggressive murlocs.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Before the Third War, the Dawning Isles were known as scenic keys resting on the calm, clear waters of Lordamere Lake. When the Plague of Undeath swept across Lordaeron, corruption seeped into the lake's shallows. The vegetation turned pallid and rotting, driving away idyllic peacefulness. Today, the Vile Fin murloc tribe dominates the muddy shores and tangled brush, aggressively defending their burgeoning colonies from anyone seeking to traverse the lake.",["t"]="Blight on the Lake"},{["b"]="Murlocs were not always the only danger on the isles. Bog beasts once prowled the blighted islets alongside them, but the bog beasts have since vanished. In their absence the Vile Fin population has swelled to the point that the murlocs now control the isles outright, turning what was once a quiet chain of keys into their stronghold on Lordamere Lake.",["t"]="A Murloc Stronghold"}}}}}
t["subzone:dawning-wood-catacombs"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="22,245,18.602.0,45.180.0,32.215.0,48.221.0,42.206.0",["h"]="2177d9",["n"]="Catacumbas del Bosque Aurora",["s"]="Catacumbas del Bosque Aurora. Talladas en las profundidades del Cementerio del Cerro del Cuervo, las Catacumbas del Bosque Aurora son un oscuro laberinto repleto de los no-muertos más feroces de Bosque del Ocaso. Quienes se atreven a adentrarse en los túneles subterráneos se enfrentan a enjambres atrincherados de guardianes esqueléticos y necrófagos devoradores de carne. Mucho antes de que la maldición crepuscular se asentara sobre el bosque, las Catacumbas del Bosque Aurora servían como un gran lugar de descanso para los difuntos ilustres de Grand Hamlets y las granjas circundantes. Ahora sepultados bajo las ruinas del Cementerio del Cerro del Cuervo, estos oscuros pasillos de piedra albergan a los no-muertos más letales de la región. Las catacumbas cuentan con dos alas subterráneas distintas: los pasadizos occidentales están ocupados por hileras de esqueletos reanimados que custodian tumbas ancestrales, mientras que los orientales descienden hacia una fétida madriguera atestada de necrófagos voraces y portadores de enfermedades. Los viajeros solitarios rara vez sobreviven en sus profundidades.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Paladin"]="The catacombs are a grim testament to the fallen of the kingdom, demanding that the holy wrath of the Light cleanse the desecrated tombs.",["class:Priest"]="Beneath the stone vaults of Raven Hill, restless spirits and decaying corpses cry out for final rest, making the catacombs a somber trial of faith."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The catacombs lie directly beneath Raven Hill Cemetery, on the far western edge of Duskwood. Entrances descend from the surface among the sprawling grave markers and ruined crypts.",["al"]={"catacombs location","where is dawning wood catacombs","how to get to catacombs"},["q"]="Where are the Dawning Wood Catacombs located?"},{["a"]="The catacombs harbor the most concentrated and ferocious undead in Duskwood. The western wing is defended by heavily armed skeletal warriors, while the eastern tunnels are infested with savage, plague-ridden ghouls.",["al"]={"catacombs enemies","what is in dawning wood catacombs","catacomb monsters"},["q"]="What lurks inside the catacombs?"},{["a"]="Back when the region was still the verdant Brightwood, the catacombs were excavated as a grand burial vault for local families and luminaries. The dark curse that later engulfed the woods reanimated those entombed within.",["al"]={"catacombs history","why build catacombs","original purpose of catacombs"},["q"]="Why were the catacombs built in the first place?"},{["a"]="Venturing into the catacombs alone is perilous. The claustrophobic tunnels offer little room to retreat, and the undead pack tightly together in aggressive swarms capable of overwhelming isolated travelers.",["al"]={"can i solo catacombs","catacombs danger","is catacombs hard"},["q"]="Is it safe to explore the catacombs alone?"}},["kw"]={"crypts","dawning wood catacombs","duskwood","ghouls","raven hill cemetery","skeletons","undead"},["n"]="Dawning Wood Catacombs",["s"]="Carved deep beneath Raven Hill Cemetery, the Dawning Wood Catacombs are a dark labyrinth teeming with the fiercest undead in Duskwood. Those who brave the subterranean tunnels face entrenched swarms of skeletal guardians and flesh-eating ghouls.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Long before the twilight curse settled over the forest, the Dawning Wood Catacombs served as a grand resting place for the honored dead of Grand Hamlets and the surrounding homesteads. Now buried beneath the ruined Raven Hill Cemetery, these dark stone corridors hold the most lethal undead in the region. The catacombs feature two distinct subterranean wings: the western passages are held by ranks of animated skeletons guarding ancestral tombs, while the eastern passages descend into a foul warren overrun by ravenous, disease-bearing ghouls. Lone travelers rarely survive deep within their depths.",["t"]="Beneath Raven Hill"}}}}}
t["subzone:dead-acre"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="9,279,19.446.0,39.213.0,51.282.0,31.148.0",["h"]="18645b",["n"]="El Campo Funesto",["s"]="El Campo Funesto. El Campo Funesto es una granja en ruinas que todavía humea en el sureste de Páramos de Poniente, cerca del puente sobre el río hacia Bosque del Ocaso. Reducidos a cenizas por la Hermandad Defias durante su levantamiento por toda la región, sus campos ennegrecidos están ahora desiertos de vida humana y acechados por gólems de la cosecha rebeldes. Situado justo al norte del camino que une Colina del Centinela con Bosque del Ocaso, El Campo Funesto fue antaño una próspera hacienda entre los fértiles campos de Páramos de Poniente. Cuando la Hermandad Defias se alzó en armas y expulsó a los terratenientes locales, esta granja encontró un final violento. La vivienda y los cultivos circundantes fueron reducidos a cenizas, dejando tras de sí maderos carbonizados, tierra humeante y Vigías de la cosecha mecánicos que siguen cosechando sin descanso el suelo estéril.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="The Dead Acre stands as a grim reminder of Stormwind's neglect in Westfall, leaving loyal farmers defenseless against the violent depredations of the Defias Brotherhood."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Defias Brotherhood burned the farmstead and its surrounding fields to the ground when taking control of Westfall. The farm earned its grim name from the blackened ruins and smoldering earth left in their wake.",["al"]={"why dead acre","what happened to dead acre","why is it burned"},["q"]="Why is this place called the Dead Acre?"},{["a"]="Like many farms across Westfall, the mechanical reapers built to tend the crops were left behind when the settlers fled or died. Corrupted or left without caretakers, the automated Harvest Watchers continue to endlessly patrol the burned-out fields, attacking anyone who draws near.",["al"]={"harvest golems dead acre","why are there golems","harvest watchers"},["q"]="Why are mechanical Harvest Watchers wandering here?"},{["a"]="The Dead Acre sits in southeastern Westfall, nestled just north of the main road near the bridge that crosses into the shadowed borders of Duskwood.",["al"]={"dead acre location","where is dead acre","how to find dead acre"},["q"]="Where is the Dead Acre located?"}},["kw"]={"burned farm","dead acre","defias","farm","harvest watcher","westfall"},["n"]="Dead Acre",["s"]="The Dead Acre is a ruined, smoldering farmstead in southeastern Westfall near the river bridge to Duskwood. Burned to ash by the Defias Brotherhood during their uprising across the countryside, the blackened fields are now abandoned by people and stalked by rogue harvest golems.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Situated just north of the road linking Sentinel Hill to Duskwood, the Dead Acre was once a productive homestead among the breadbasket farms of Westfall. When the Defias Brotherhood rose in revolt and drove out the local landowners, this farm met a violent end. The homestead and its surrounding crops were put to the torch, leaving behind scorched timber, smoking earth, and wandering mechanical Harvest Watchers that still reap the barren soil.",["t"]="Ashes on the Border"}}}}}
t["subzone:dead-field"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="10,327,25.616.0,20.386.1,23.196.0,33.202.0,17.220.0,37.198.0",["h"]="16b24a",["n"]="El Campo Muerto",["s"]="El Campo Muerto. El Campo Muerto es una granja abandonada y asolada situada en el norte del Bosque de Argénteos. Antaño una tranquila tierra de labranza rural, ha sido tomada por los gnolls Putrepellejo y convertida en una base avanzada para las fuerzas de la Plaga. Los repetidos intentos de los Renegados por despejar la zona han fracasado bajo el mando de la banshee Nightlash. Poco queda de la granja original en los confines septentrionales del Bosque de Argénteos, pues sus antiguos ocupantes vivos sucumbieron hace mucho a la Tercera Guerra. Hoy en día, la parcela en ruinas sirve como base de operaciones para los gnolls Putrepellejo, que actúan como devotos sirvientes de la Plaga. A medida que su número aumentaba, los exploradores Mortacechadores que pasaban por la región detectaron indicios de una inminente movilización militar que amenazaba las líneas de suministro y los puestos avanzados de los Renegados. Pequeños asaltos de los Renegados contra la granja han fracasado repetidamente, repelidos por la aullante aparición Nightlash, una banshee que se manifiesta cada vez que sus esclavos gnolls se ven en peligro.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Rogue"]="Deathstalker recon teams monitor the farm closely; infiltrating the gnoll ranks and striking their command structure is a critical tactical priority.",["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, the Scourge foothold at the Dead Field poses an immediate threat to the road between the Sepulcher and northern Lordaeron, demanding swift extermination."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Dead Field is a decrepit, blighted farmstead located in northern Silverpine Forest. Once an ordinary human farm, it has fallen into ruin and is now occupied by Scourge-aligned Rot Hide gnolls.",["al"]={"dead field silverpine","where is dead field","what happened to dead field"},["q"]="What is the Dead Field?"},{["a"]="These Rot Hide gnolls are under the sway of the Scourge. They use the farmstead as a forward staging ground to gather forces and prepare attacks against Forsaken positions in northern Silverpine Forest.",["al"]={"why rot hide gnolls","rot hides dead field","scourge gnolls"},["q"]="Why are there gnolls at the farm?"},{["a"]="Nightlash is a Scourge banshee commanding the Rot Hide gnolls at the farm. Whenever Forsaken strike forces assault the encampment, she materializes to defend her servants, repelling previous attempts to reclaim the land.",["al"]={"nightlash banshee","banshee in dead field","who protects the gnolls"},["q"]="Who is Nightlash?"},{["a"]="The encampment answers to Thule Ravenclaw, a powerful necromancer operating from nearby Fenris Isle. He coordinates the gnolls through apparitions and magical oversight to harass Forsaken expansion.",["al"]={"who controls dead field","thule ravenclaw dead field","who is in charge"},["q"]="Who commands the Scourge forces here?"}},["kw"]={"banshee","dead field","deathstalkers","nightlash","rot hide","silverpine forest","thule ravenclaw"},["n"]="Dead Field",["s"]="The Dead Field is a blighted, abandoned farmstead situated in northern Silverpine Forest. Once quiet rural farmland, it has been seized by the Rot Hide gnolls and transformed into a forward staging ground for Scourge forces. Repeated Forsaken attempts to clear the area have faltered under the command of the banshee Nightlash.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Little remains of the original farmstead in the northern reaches of Silverpine Forest, its previous living occupants long lost to the Third War. Today, the ruined plot serves as a base of operations for the Rot Hide gnolls, who act as willing servants to the Scourge. As their numbers swelled, Deathstalker scouts passing through the region noted signs of imminent military mobilization threatening Forsaken supply lines and outposts. Small Forsaken assaults against the farm have repeatedly failed, turned back by the wailing apparition Nightlash—a banshee who manifests whenever her gnoll thralls are endangered.",["t"]="A Blighted Staging Ground"},{["b"]="The Rot Hide gnolls do not act alone. Their operations in the Dead Field are orchestrated from afar by the necromancer Thule Ravenclaw, based out of Fenris Isle. Intending to assert Scourge dominance over Silverpine and drive Sylvanas's forces out of Lordaeron, Ravenclaw projects magical apparitions to the farmstead to survey his undead horde and issue warnings to Forsaken intruders.",["t"]="Ravenclaw's Ambition"}}}}}
t["subzone:deadeye-shore"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,271,34.569.0,31.205.0,30.263.0,44.243.0",["h"]="cd6e2c",["n"]="Costa de Mortojo",["s"]="Costa de Mortojo. Costa de Mortojo es un tramo de costa azotado por el viento en el extremo oriental de Durotar, directamente al este de Barranco Árido. Nombrada en memoria del legendario caudillo de Bleeding Hollow, Kilrogg Deadeye, por sus áridas arenas merodean principalmente rapaces salvajes, escórpidos y jabalíes ferales. Extendiéndose bajo los riscos rojos del centro de Durotar, Costa de Mortojo toma su nombre de Kilrogg Deadeye, el caudillo tuerto del clan Bleeding Hollow que luchó en la Primera y Segunda Guerra. Desde las alturas, la arena y los afloramientos rocosos recuerdan levemente la forma de una calavera a la que le falta una cuenca ocular. Aunque carece de asentamientos importantes o puestos militares, la costa dista mucho de ser pacífica: la fauna agresiva domina las arenas, y se sabe que siniestros cultores de Filo Ardiente bajan hacia el agua desde sus escondites cercanos en los barrancos.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["race:Orc"]="For orcs establishing their new nation in Durotar, the shore honors Kilrogg Deadeye, reminding them of the old chieftains who shaped the Horde's history during the wars on Azeroth."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The shoreline is named after Kilrogg Deadeye, the famed chieftain of the Bleeding Hollow clan. The natural coastal terrain also resembles a skull missing an eye, echoing the chieftain's own blinded socket.",["al"]={"who is deadeye","why deadeye shore","origin of name"},["q"]="Why is it called Deadeye Shore?"},{["a"]="No permanent settlements stand on Deadeye Shore. The stretch of coast is inhabited primarily by native wildlife like raptors, scorpids, and boars, though fishermen and travelers occasionally pass through—sometimes running afoul of hidden Burning Blade cultists.",["al"]={"who is here","settlements deadeye shore","npcs deadeye"},["q"]="Who lives along Deadeye Shore?"},{["a"]="Beyond aggressive local beasts, the greatest danger comes from the neighboring Drygulch Ravine. Cultists belonging to the Burning Blade occasionally wander down from the rocky canyons toward the coast, ambushing unwary travelers and fishermen.",["al"]={"dangers deadeye shore","enemies here","burning blade deadeye"},["q"]="What threats are found around Deadeye Shore?"}},["kw"]={"bleeding hollow","deadeye shore","drygulch ravine","durotar","kilrogg deadeye"},["n"]="Deadeye Shore",["s"]="Deadeye Shore is a windswept stretch of coastline along Durotar's eastern edge, directly east of Drygulch Ravine. Named in memory of the legendary Bleeding Hollow chieftain Kilrogg Deadeye, the barren sands are roamed primarily by wild raptors, scorpids, and feral boars.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Stretching beneath the red bluffs of central Durotar, Deadeye Shore takes its name from Kilrogg Deadeye, the one-eyed chieftain of the Bleeding Hollow clan who fought in the First and Second Wars. From high above, the sand and rocky outcrops faintly mirror the shape of a skull with a missing eye socket. While lacking major settlements or military outposts, the shoreline is far from peaceful: aggressive wildlife dominates the sands, and shadowy cultists from the Burning Blade have been known to prowl down toward the water from their nearby hideouts in the ravines.",["t"]="A Shoreline of the Bleeding Hollow"}}}}}
t["subzone:deathknell"] = {["faq"]={{["a"]="No todos los cadáveres levantados tras la Tercera Guerra se liberaron con la mente intacta. La plaza del pueblo y la forja del norte están infestadas por los «Descerebrados»: zombis salvajes, necrófagos y esqueletos aún impulsados por la voluntad residual y persistente de la Plaga. Los defensores renegados los eliminan periódicamente para recuperar equipo y defender la iglesia.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="492b6d",["i"]=2,["q"]="",["sp"]=0},{["a"]="Un destacamento de la Cruzada Escarlata mantiene un campamento en las colinas al sureste de la aldea. Dedicados con fanatismo a destruir a todos los no-muertos indiscriminadamente, vigilan el paso, emboscan a los Renegados recién despertados e intercambian información de reconocimiento con las fortalezas escarlata de otras partes de Lordaeron.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="d29a37",["i"]=3,["q"]="",["sp"]=0},{["a"]="Hoya Nocturácnidas, la mina de oro situada en los riscos al noroeste de la aldea, está completamente invadida por arañas agresivas. Asegurar recursos naturales como el oro es fundamental para el esfuerzo bélico de los Renegados, pero hasta que no se erradique la plaga, el asentamiento no puede explotar la veta.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="64fc92",["i"]=4,["q"]="",["sp"]=0}},["fp"]="10,405,22.740.0,20.560.0,36.169.0,55.350.0,50.302.0,47.283.0",["h"]="69716d",["n"]="Camposanto",["s"]="Camposanto. Camposanto es una aldea fortificada enclavada en un valle apartado al suroeste de Claros de Tirisfal. Sirve como el principal lugar de despertar para los no-muertos recién liberados que se zafan del yugo del Rey Exánime para unirse a los Renegados. Asediado por restos descerebrados de la Plaga, fanáticos locales y una fauna agresiva, el asentamiento es un duro campo de pruebas para quienes reclaman un lugar en el reino de Sylvanas Brisaveloz. Escondido tras colinas escarpadas justo al norte de la frontera con Silverpine, Camposanto es donde los no-muertos recién despertados abren por primera vez los ojos a su sombría realidad. A diferencia de la mayoría de los asentamientos de Claros de Tirisfal, que conservaron sus nombres humanos del caído Reino de Lordaeron, Camposanto fue rebautizado de forma explícita por los no-muertos que lo reclamaron. El pueblo en sí está dividido en dos: los Renegados se aferran tenazmente a los terrenos del sur alrededor de la vieja iglesia, mientras que la mitad norte, incluida la forja de la aldea, permanece invadida por zombis descerebrados de la Plaga y necrófagos salvajes. Guardianes de la muerte de élite mantienen el estrecho desfiladero fuera del valle firmemente sellado contra intrusos, lo que permite a los cuidadores locales incorporar a los recién llegados al servicio de la Reina Alma en Pena.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="Though isolated and dark, this valley is the gateway to the Forsaken kingdom, supplying fresh soldiers to bolster the Horde's foothold in the Eastern Kingdoms.",["race:Undead"]="Every Forsaken adventurer begins here, rising from the cold earth of the Shadow Grave to find purpose and shelter under Lady Sylvanas after the horror of the Plague."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Deathknell was renamed after it became an undead settlement, unlike most communities in Tirisfal that retained their human names. The reason for the new name is unknown.",["al"]={"deathknell name origin","why is it called deathknell","old name of deathknell"},["q"]="Why was the town renamed Deathknell?"},{["a"]="Not every corpse raised in the wake of the Third War broke free with their minds intact. The northern village square and forge are infested by the 'Mindless Ones'—feral zombies, ghouls, and skeletons still driven by the residual, lingering will of the Scourge. Forsaken defenders regularly clear them out to salvage equipment and defend the church.",["al"]={"why are zombies in deathknell","scourge in deathknell","mindless ones deathknell"},["q"]="Why is the northern half of the town overrun by undead?"},{["a"]="A detachment of the Scarlet Crusade maintains an encampment in the hills southeast of the village. Fanatically dedicated to destroying all undead indiscriminately, they monitor the pass, ambush newly awakened Forsaken, and exchange scouting intelligence with Scarlet strongholds elsewhere in Lordaeron.",["al"]={"scarlet camp deathknell","crusaders outside deathknell","scarlet crusade tirisfal valley"},["q"]="What is the Scarlet Crusade doing near Deathknell?"},{["a"]="Night Web's Hollow, the gold mine situated in the cliffs northwest of the village, is completely overrun by aggressive spiders. Securing natural resources like gold is critical for the Forsaken war effort, but until the infestation is cleared, the settlement cannot exploit the vein.",["al"]={"deathknell mine","night webs hollow","spider mine tirisfal"},["q"]="Why can't the Forsaken use the local gold mine?"}},["kw"]={"deathknell","forsaken starting area","mindless ones","night web's hollow","shadow grave","sylvanas","tirisfal glades"},["n"]="Deathknell",["s"]="Deathknell is a fortified village nestled in a secluded valley in southwestern Tirisfal Glades. It serves as the primary awakening grounds for newly freed undead breaking free from the Lich King's grasp to join the Forsaken. Besieged by mindless Scourge remnants, local zealots, and aggressive wildlife, the settlement is a harsh proving ground for those claiming a place in Sylvanas Windrunner's kingdom.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Tucked away behind jagged hills just north of the Silverpine border, Deathknell is where newly awakened undead first open their eyes to their bleak reality. Unlike most settlements in Tirisfal Glades that preserved their human names from the fallen Kingdom of Lordaeron, Deathknell was explicitly renamed by the undead who claimed it. The town itself is cleaved in two: the Forsaken cling stubbornly to the southern grounds around the old church, while the northern half—including the village forge—remains overrun by mindless Scourge zombies and feral ghouls. Elite Deathguards keep the narrow gorge out of the valley securely sealed against intruders, allowing local caretakers to induct new arrivals into the Banshee Queen's service.",["t"]="Cradle of the Forsaken"},{["b"]="Survival in Deathknell is precarious. To the northwest, Night Web's Hollow—a gold mine vital for the Forsaken's fledgling economy—has been lost to monstrous spiders. To the southeast, an aggressive encampment of the Scarlet Crusade maintains constant watch, trading couriers with their strongholds to the east and probing the valley's defenses. Meanwhile, the village caretakers must continually fight off the mindless undead wandering the northern ruins while gathering scrap metal, tools, and supplies to equip newly arisen souls for the long road ahead.",["t"]="A Valley Under Siege"}}}}}
t["subzone:decrepit-ferry"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,288,20.523.0,21.349.0,48.241.0,44.175.0,46.158.0,51.155.0",["h"]="c1c7d1",["n"]="El Viejo Embarcadero",["s"]="El Viejo Embarcadero. El Viejo Embarcadero es un muelle en ruinas en la orilla oriental del Bosque de Argénteos que antaño permitía cruzar el Lago Lordamere hacia la Isla de Fenris. Tras la caída de Lordaeron, el transbordador fue destruido, su barquero asesinado y la costa invadida por no-muertos y despiadados gnolls Putrapiel. Antes de la Tercera Guerra, este muelle bullía con el tráfico diario a través del Lago Lordamere. Los granjeros locales llevaban productos frescos hasta la orilla, vendiendo sus cosechas directamente al acaudalado señor de la Isla de Fenris y a su séquito. Por una módica tarifa, el barquero transportaba mercancías, mensajeros y nobles de visita de un lado a otro entre tierra firme y el torreón. Ese comercio pacífico terminó abruptamente cuando la Plaga arrasó el reino. El barquero fue asesinado brutalmente, las barcas quedaron destrozadas y el embarcadero cayó en la decadencia.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["race:Undead"]="The ruins are a grim reminder of Lordaeron's fall, now overrun by mind-numbing Scourge remnants and filthy gnolls that threaten Forsaken operations in eastern Silverpine."},["faq"]={{["a"]="It was the main crossing point between mainland Silverpine and Fenris Isle. Local farmers used the ferry to haul their harvests across Lordamere Lake to sell to the island's noble lord, paying the local ferryman a small fare for each voyage.",["al"]={"ferry history","what was this dock","why is there a ferry here"},["q"]="What was the Decrepit Ferry used for originally?"},{["a"]="When the Scourge invaded Lordaeron, the dock was attacked. The ferryman was murdered, the boats and crossing gear were destroyed, and the location was abandoned to the undead.",["al"]={"what happened to ferryman","who broke the ferry"},["q"]="What happened to the ferry and its ferryman?"},{["a"]="The shoreline is infested with remnants of the Scourge, including ghouls and skeletal warriors, alongside dangerous Rot Hide gnolls prowling the nearby banks.",["al"]={"decrepit ferry mobs","what lives at the ferry"},["q"]="What monsters lurk around the ferry docks now?"},{["a"]="No. The ferry was wrecked during the invasion and lies in ruins. Anyone wishing to reach Fenris Isle must swim or find alternative passage across the lake.",["al"]={"take boat to fenris","how to get to fenris isle","does the ferry work"},["q"]="Can you still take a boat to Fenris Isle from here?"}},["kw"]={"decrepit ferry","fenris isle","ferryman","ghouls","lordamere lake","rot hide","scourge","silverpine forest"},["n"]="Decrepit Ferry",["s"]="The Decrepit Ferry is a ruined dock on the eastern shore of Silverpine Forest that once provided passage across Lordamere Lake to Fenris Isle. Following the fall of Lordaeron, the ferry was destroyed, its operator murdered, and the shoreline overrun by undead and vicious Rot Hide gnolls.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Before the Third War, this dock bustled with daily traffic across Lordamere Lake. Local farmers brought fresh produce down to the water, selling their crops directly to the wealthy lord of Fenris Isle and his household. For a modest fee, the ferryman carried trade goods, messengers, and visiting nobles back and forth between the mainland and the keep. That peaceful commerce ended abruptly when the Scourge swept through the kingdom. The ferryman was brutally killed, the boats were smashed, and the pier fell into decay.",["t"]="A Lifeline Cut Short"},{["b"]="Today, the docks are a hazard to any traveler passing along the lake shore. With the ferry out of commission, Fenris Isle sits isolated across the water, while the ruins themselves crawl with ghouls, skeletal warriors, and roving Rot Hide gnolls. What was once an orderly point of transit has become another festering pocket of danger in Silverpine.",["t"]="A Corrupted Shoreline"}}}}}
t["subzone:deep-elem-mine"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,224,15.397.0,29.457.1,30.188.0,48.257.0,24.243.0,37.196.0",["h"]="4cefa6",["n"]="Mina de Elem",["s"]="Mina de Elem. Mina de Elem es un lugar de excavación enclavado en el corazón de Bosque de Argénteos. En su día fue una explotación activa, pero quedó arrasada cuando la magia oscura del Archimago Arugal barrió la región, transformando a sus mineros en salvajes huargen. Situada en el centro de Bosque de Argénteos, Mina de Elem sirvió antaño a los habitantes vivos de Lordaeron como un filón ordinario de recursos. Cuando el Archimago Arugal desató la pesadilla lupina sobre el bosque, su maldición feral se extendió hasta las profundidades de los túneles. Los peones del interior sucumbieron a la aflicción, convirtiéndose en feroces huargen que abandonaron sus picos para reclamar la caverna como una guarida depredadora.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["profession:Mining"]="Though currently hazardous due to the feral pack residing within, the mine represents one of Silverpine's richest subterranean mineral deposits.",["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, securing the mine is both an economic necessity and a direct mandate from the Sepulcher to break Arugal's encroaching grip on central Silverpine."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The mine is infested with hostile worgen afflicted by Archmage Arugal's magic. They are led by their former human foreman, Grimson the Pale, who now rules the pack deep within the tunnels.",["al"]={"whats in deep elem mine","deep elem mine mobs","who lives in deep elem mine"},["q"]="What is inside Deep Elem Mine?"},{["a"]="The Forsaken seek to exploit the mine's natural mineral wealth to bolster their war efforts in Lordaeron. Dalar Dawnweaver and the leadership at the Sepulcher intend to claim its resources in the name of Dreadlord Varimathras once the worgen are eradicated.",["al"]={"forsaken mine interest","why clear deep elem mine","who wants the mine"},["q"]="Why do the Forsaken want Deep Elem Mine cleared?"},{["a"]="Grimson was originally the mortal foreman overseeing operations at Deep Elem Mine. After Arugal's feral curse transformed the workers, Grimson became a cunning worgen alpha who retained enough intellect to command the pack inhabiting the mine.",["al"]={"who is grimson","grimson the pale lore","deep elem mine boss"},["q"]="Who is Grimson the Pale?"},{["a"]="They were not outsiders who moved in; the original miners were transformed by the spread of Archmage Arugal's curse across Silverpine Forest, turning the workforce into monsters where they worked.",["al"]={"why are there worgen in the mine","worgen origin deep elem mine","how did miners turn"},["q"]="How did the worgen get into the mine?"}},["kw"]={"arugal","dalar dawnweaver","deep elem mine","grimson the pale","silverpine forest","varimathras","worgen"},["n"]="Deep Elem Mine",["s"]="Deep Elem Mine is an excavation site nestled in the heart of Silverpine Forest. Once an active operation, it was overrun when Archmage Arugal's dark magic swept through the region, transforming its miners into savage worgen.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Situated central to Silverpine Forest, the Deep Elem Mine once served the living inhabitants of Lordaeron as an ordinary resource vein. When Archmage Arugal unleashed the lupine nightmare upon the forest, his feral curse spread deep into the tunnels. The laborers inside succumbed to the affliction, turning into vicious worgen who abandoned their pickaxes to claim the cavern as a predatory lair.",["t"]="A Den of Beasts"},{["b"]="The pack within the mine is commanded by Grimson the Pale, the former mine foreman who retained his cunning even after his monstrous transformation. Recognizing the strategic value of the tunnels and their ore, the Forsaken at the Sepulcher take a keen interest in reclaiming the site. Under orders backed by the authority of Dreadlord Varimathras, Forsaken agents seek to sever Grimson's head and purge the beasts so the Horde can secure the mine's wealth.",["t"]="Grimson and Forsaken Ambition"}}}}}
t["subzone:deeprun-tram"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="12,410,36.774.0,31.306.0,36.317.0,44.293.0,25.192.0",["h"]="9636bd",["n"]="Tren subterráneo",["s"]="Tren subterráneo. El Tren subterráneo es una maravilla subterránea de la ingeniería gnoma que une las capitales de la Alianza de Forjaz y Ciudad de Ventormenta. Encargado por el Rey Magni Barbabronce tras la Segunda Guerra, permite a ciudadanos y soldados recorrer grandes distancias bajo tierra en cuestión de minutos. Las vías dobles cerradas atraviesan montañas y lagos subterráneos, sirviendo como una arteria vital para el comercio y el apoyo militar de la Alianza. Tras la devastación de la Segunda Guerra, el Rey Magni Barbabronce se sentía cada vez más frustrado por la lentitud con la que la ayuda enana y los suministros de construcción llegaban a Ventormenta a través de los pasos montañosos. Para solventar este obstáculo logístico y garantizar que los soldados enanos pudieran reforzar rápidamente la capital humana en tiempos de crisis, Magni recurrió al Manitas Mayor Gelbin Mekkatorque. El maestro ingeniero gnomo trazó los planos de un ferrocarril subterráneo cerrado impulsado por tecnología puntera. A pesar de las complicaciones durante la excavación —que incluyeron atravesar un inmenso lago subterráneo y lidiar con incesantes plagas de ratas de las profundidades—, el tren se convirtió en uno de los mayores logros de la Alianza, transportando gratis a miles de viajeros entre Forjaz y Ventormenta.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="The tram serves as the primary strategic artery connecting the Alliance's two most fortified capitals, allowing for rapid troop redeployment and mutual defense within minutes.",["profession:Engineering"]="The entire railway is an unparalleled gnomish masterpiece, showcasing advanced track propulsion, pressurized glasswork capable of withstanding subterranean lake depths, and intricate electrical switching stations."},["faq"]={{["a"]="After the Second War, King Magni Bronzebeard needed a faster way to transport supplies and dwarven troops to assist in rebuilding and defending Stormwind. He commissioned High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque, who drafted and executed the subterranean railway project to seamlessly bind the two capitals together.",["al"]={"why build the tram","tram purpose","who built deeprun tram"},["q"]="Why was the Deeprun Tram built?"},{["a"]="During the excavation between Dun Morogh and Stormwind, gnomish engineers breached a massive subterranean lake. Rather than routing around it, they constructed a sealed, reinforced glass viewing tunnel directly through the deep water, allowing passengers to watch wild threshadons and sharks swim alongside the track.",["al"]={"tram water window","underwater tram","deeprun tram lake"},["q"]="How does the tram travel underwater?"},{["a"]="The damp, dark subterranean shafts provide an ideal breeding ground for vermin. Gnomish station masters constantly struggle to keep the rat population from chewing through cables or overrunning the platforms, occasionally relying on travelers and rat catchers like Monty to cull their numbers.",["al"]={"deeprun rats","why rats in tram","rat problem"},["q"]="Why are there so many rats along the tracks?"},{["a"]="Yes. Sponsored as an open civic and military project by the governments of Ironforge and Stormwind, the tram operates continuously and without fare for all citizens and allies of the Alliance.",["al"]={"tram cost","tram ticket price","how much to ride tram"},["q"]="Is the tram free to ride?"}},["kw"]={"deeprun tram","dwarven district","gelbin mekkatorque","magni bronzebeard","subterranean lake","subway","tinkertown","tram"},["n"]="Deeprun Tram",["s"]="The Deeprun Tram is an subterranean marvel of gnomish engineering linking the Alliance capitals of Ironforge and Stormwind City. Commissioned by King Magni Bronzebeard following the Second War, it allows citizens and soldiers to cross vast distances beneath the earth in mere minutes. The enclosed twin tracks cut beneath mountain and lake, serving as a vital artery for Alliance military support and commerce.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Following the devastation of the Second War, King Magni Bronzebeard grew increasingly frustrated with how slowly dwarven aid and construction supplies reached Stormwind across the mountain passes. To solve the logistical hurdle and guarantee that dwarven soldiers could rapidly reinforce the human capital in times of crisis, Magni turned to High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque. The master gnomish engineer drafted designs for an enclosed underground railway powered by cutting-edge technology. Despite excavation complications—including cutting right through a vast subterranean lake and battling relentless infestations of underground rats—the tram became a crowning achievement of the Alliance, moving thousands of travelers free of charge between Ironforge and Stormwind.",["t"]="A Marvel of Subterranean Engineering"}}}}}
t["subzone:deepwater-tavern"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,353,24.710.0,38.146.0,46.202.0,43.163.0,26.239.0",["h"]="877c0a",["n"]="Mesón Aguahonda",["s"]="Mesón Aguahonda. El Mesón Aguahonda es la bulliciosa posada costera de Puerto de Menethil, enclavada en las húmedas marismas de Los Humedales. Sirve como punto de encuentro principal, lugar de reabastecimiento y descanso para viajeros y marineros que recorren la transitada ciudad portuaria. Entre abundantes tragos y rumores del puerto, los parroquianos a menudo encuentran trabajo o se topan con volátiles peleas de taberna. Ubicado en las empapadas calles de Puerto de Menethil, el Mesón Aguahonda ofrece a los viajeros un agradable refugio frente a las marismas traicioneras y en perpetua llovizna del exterior. Marineros, estibadores, mercaderes y aventureros agotados se reúnen bajo sus vigas de madera para intercambiar noticias, compartir un fuego cálido y curar sus heridas. Más allá de los servicios habituales de una posada portuaria, alberga a un instructor de primeros auxilios residente y a mercaderes locales que atienden a quienes se dirigen a los peligros de la ciénaga o se embarcan a través del Mare Magnum. El ambiente es bullicioso y en ocasiones peligroso; las disputas estallan con facilidad por una cerveza derramada, y es sabido que alborotadores notorios como Tapoke 'Slim' Jahn desatan de vez en cuando peleas en toda la taberna.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="The Deepwater Tavern serves as an indispensable rallying point and rest haven for Alliance members passing between Ironforge and the open sea."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Deepwater Tavern is situated near the waterfront of Menethil Harbor, the primary port town of the Wetlands on the western coast of Khaz Modan.",["al"]={"deepwater tavern location","where is deepwater tavern","menethil harbor inn"},["q"]="Where is the Deepwater Tavern located?"},{["a"]="Besides typical innkeeper lodging and refreshments, the tavern houses merchants and a first aid trainer, making it a critical resupply and healing point for adventurers traveling through the marshlands.",["al"]={"deepwater tavern services","menethil tavern trainers","what can i find at deepwater tavern"},["q"]="What services are available inside the tavern?"},{["a"]="The tavern is famous for spontaneous fights, with a shifty troublemaker named Tapoke 'Slim' Jahn frequently instigating brawls among the rowdy patrons and sailors.",["al"]={"bar brawl menethil","tapoke slim jahn","who starts fights at deepwater tavern"},["q"]="Who frequently starts brawls in the tavern?"},{["a"]="Menethil Harbor is the major shipping and naval gateway linking Khaz Modan to Kalimdor and northern ports. As the sole major inn in town, it gathers a steady flow of sailors, mercenaries, and Alliance adventurers heading into the Wetlands.",["al"]={"why visit deepwater tavern","why is deepwater tavern popular"},["q"]="Why is the tavern so busy?"}},["kw"]={"deepwater tavern","first aid trainer","innkeeper","menethil harbor","tapoke slim jahn","tavern brawl","wetlands"},["n"]="Deepwater Tavern",["s"]="The Deepwater Tavern is the bustling seaside inn of Menethil Harbor, nestled in the damp marshlands of the Wetlands. It serves as the primary meeting spot, resupply point, and resting place for travelers and mariners navigating the busy port town. Between hearty drinks and harbor rumors, patrons frequently find work or run into volatile tavern brawls.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Standing within the sodden streets of Menethil Harbor, the Deepwater Tavern offers travelers a welcome shelter from the perpetually drizzly, treacherous marshlands outside. Sailors, dockworkers, merchants, and weary adventurers gather beneath its timber beams to trade news, share a warm fire, and patch their wounds. Beyond the usual amenities of a harbor inn, it houses a resident first aid trainer and local merchants catering to those bound for the perils of the marsh or embarking across the Great Sea. The atmosphere is boisterous and occasionally hazardous; disputes flare up quickly over spilled ale, with notorious troublemakers like Tapoke 'Slim' Jahn known to spark the occasional tavern-wide brawl.",["t"]="Heart of Menethil Harbor"}}}}}
t["subzone:defias-hideout"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,268,17.598.0,34.252.0,47.240.0,44.174.0,48.212.0",["h"]="925296",["n"]="Escondite Defias",["s"]="Escondite Defias. Escondite Defias es una casa discreta y ruinosa situada en el extremo sur de Arroyo de la Luna. Aunque se mimetiza con el resto de este asentamiento en ruinas, su piso superior oculta la principal entrada terrestre a la extensa red subterránea de Las Minas de la Muerte. A simple vista, Escondite Defias parece una casa solariega o una granja saqueada más de Arroyo de la Luna, abarrotada de vagabundos indigentes y matones Defias. Sin embargo, su modesto interior enmascara el centro neurálgico de las operaciones en el sur de Edwin VanCleef. Al subir a la planta superior, se revela una abertura que conduce directamente al laberinto de Las Minas de la Muerte. Debido a que la Hermandad concentra su mano de obra en vigilar el perímetro de Arroyo de la Luna y en faenar en lo más profundo del subsuelo, la guarida en sí cuenta con escasa guarnición, funcionando más como un cuello de botella intensamente vigilado que como un bastión activo.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Rogue"]="The hideout is a masterclass in clandestine defense: by disguising the gateway to a massive underground fortress within a nondescript ruined manor, the Defias keep their true scale hidden from casual Stormwind patrols.",["faction:Alliance"]="This decrepit estate serves as the front door to Edwin VanCleef's conspiracy, making it a critical staging ground for Alliance adventurers seeking to put an end to the Defias rebellion."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Inside the structure lies a staircase that leads up to a winding tunnel, serving as the overland entrance to the Deadmines. Aside from wandering vagrants and scattered bandits, the building itself is mostly bare, acting primarily as a guarded entryway.",["al"]={"inside defias hideout","hideout entrance","what is here"},["q"]="What is inside the Defias Hideout?"},{["a"]="The Defias Brotherhood concentrates its fighting forces outside in the streets of Moonbrook to intercept intruders before they draw close, while the rest of their laborers and enforcers are busy working far below in the depths of the mines.",["al"]={"why empty","where are the defias","why so few guards"},["q"]="Why is the hideout relatively unguarded inside?"},{["a"]="The hideout is located on the southern edge of Moonbrook in southwestern Westfall, distinguished as a large, intact two-story building resting near the base of the mountains.",["al"]={"how to find hideout","where is defias hideout","hideout location"},["q"]="Where in Moonbrook is this building located?"},{["a"]="The building and the surrounding town are populated by Defias bandits along with desperate vagrants who have gathered in Moonbrook, having fled poverty or aligned themselves with the Brotherhood out of necessity.",["al"]={"who are vagrants","moonbrook vagrants","defias people"},["q"]="Who are the people lingering around the hideout?"}},["kw"]={"deadmines","defias","defias hideout","entrance","moonbrook","vancleef","westfall"},["n"]="Defias Hideout",["s"]="The Defias Hideout is an unassuming, derelict house situated on the southern edge of Moonbrook. Though it blends in with the surrounding ruined settlement, its upper floor conceals the primary overland entrance into the extensive subterranean network of the Deadmines.",["sec"]={{["b"]="To the casual eye, the Defias Hideout looks like any other ransacked manor or farmhouse in Moonbrook, overrun by destitute vagrants and Defias thugs. However, its modest interior masks the nerve center of Edwin VanCleef's southern operations. Ascending to the upper floor reveals an opening that leads directly down into the sprawling labyrinth of the Deadmines. Because the Brotherhood focuses its manpower on guarding the perimeter of Moonbrook and laboring deep underground, the hideout itself is sparsely garrisoned, functioning more as a heavily monitored bottleneck than an active stronghold.",["t"]="A Gateway in Ruin"}}}}}
t["subzone:demon-fall-canyon"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="17,274,21.577.0,28.436.0,43.141.0,46.275.0,46.193.0,36.176.0",["h"]="7209d0",["n"]="Barranco del Demonio",["s"]="Barranco del Demonio. El Barranco del Demonio es un desfiladero marcado y corrompido por la energía vil situado en el sur de Vallefresno. Señala el legendario campo de batalla donde Grommash Grito Infernal y Thrall se enfrentaron al señor del foso Mannoroth, poniendo fin a la maldición de sangre demoníaca que había esclavizado a la raza orca durante una generación. Tallado en las abruptas fronteras meridionales de Vallefresno, cerca del Cerro Lumbrevil y de la Cresta del Demonio, este cañón exhibe las profundas cicatrices de la Tercera Guerra. Fue aquí donde el Jefe de Guerra Thrall y el caudillo Grommash Grito Infernal rastrearon al señor del foso Mannoroth para romper su dominio sobre la Horda. Durante el feroz duelo, Mannoroth incapacitó a Thrall, pero Grom aprovechó la oportunidad para clavar su hacha, Aullavísceras, directamente en el pecho del demonio. La consiguiente explosión infernal destrozó al señor del foso y también mató a Grom, liberando permanentemente a los orcos de su persistente servidumbre demoníaca.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="This scorched ground is sacred to the Horde as the site of Grommash Hellscream's ultimate sacrifice, where the blood curse of the Burning Legion was finally broken.",["race:Orc"]="Every orc owes their spiritual and physical freedom to the battle fought in this canyon, where Grom traded his life to shatter their demonic bondage."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The canyon was named by the Horde to commemorate the death of the pit lord Mannoroth, who fell here after being slain by Grommash Hellscream.",["al"]={"demon fall canyon name origin","why called demon fall canyon","how did it get its name"},["q"]="Why is this place called Demon Fall Canyon?"},{["a"]="Thrall and Grom confronted Mannoroth together. Thrall was knocked unconscious, but Grom dealt a lethal blow with his axe. The violent explosion of demonic fire released by Mannoroth's demise fatally wounded Grom, freeing his people from the blood curse with his dying breath.",["al"]={"grom death","grom vs mannoroth","how did grom die"},["q"]="What happened between Grom and Mannoroth here?"},{["a"]="When the pit lord Mannoroth died, the tremendous blast of demonic energy permanently corrupted the canyon floor, leaving behind lingering fel corruption that attracts and harbors lesser demons.",["al"]={"why demons in demon fall","demon fall canyon mobs","why is it fel corrupted"},["q"]="Why are there still demons roaming the canyon?"},{["a"]="A memorial monument honoring Grom Hellscream stands nearby in the vicinity of Demon Fall Canyon, where Horde pilgrims come to pay tribute to the warrior who freed their people.",["al"]={"grom monument location","hellscream memorial","where is grom's grave"},["q"]="Where is Grom Hellscream's memorial?"}},["kw"]={"ashenvale","blood curse","demon fall canyon","gorehowl","grommash hellscream","mannoroth","pit lord","thrall"},["n"]="Demon Fall Canyon",["s"]="Demon Fall Canyon is a scarred, fel-corrupted gorge situated in southern Ashenvale. It marks the legendary battleground where Grommash Hellscream and Thrall confronted the pit lord Mannoroth, ending the demonic blood curse that had enslaved the orcish race for a generation.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Carved into the rugged southern borders of Ashenvale near Felfire Hill and Demon Fall Ridge, this canyon bears the heavy scars of the Third War. It was here that Warchief Thrall and chieftain Grommash Hellscream tracked down the pit lord Mannoroth to break his hold over the Horde. During the fierce duel, Mannoroth incapacitated Thrall, but Grom seized the opening to drive his axe, Gorehowl, straight into the demon's chest. The resulting infernal explosion shattered the pit lord and slew Grom as well, permanently liberating the orcs from their lingering demonic servitude.",["t"]="The Fall of Mannoroth"},{["b"]="Following Mannoroth's demise, the Horde dubbed the canyon to commemorate Grom's final stand, erecting a monument nearby to honor his redemption. Despite the pit lord's destruction, his violent death unleashed raw demonic power that thoroughly tainted the surrounding land. Today, the canyon remains saturated in fel magic and crawls with hostile lingering lesser demons, making any pilgrimage to this hallowed ground a perilous venture.",["t"]="A Sacred Yet Dangerous Chasm"}}}}}
t["subzone:demon-fall-ridge"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,252,23.462.0,21.389.0,26.149.0,35.246.0,26.148.0,44.182.0",["h"]="bb087a",["n"]="Cresta del Demonio",["s"]="Cresta del Demonio. Cresta del Demonio es una meseta asolada en el sureste de Vallefresno, con vistas al cañón donde cayó Mannoroth. Plagada de demonios menores y magia corruptora, la cresta se centra en torno a un cubil de túmulos de los elfos de la noche profanado y reclamado por la Legión Ardiente. Elevándose directamente al oeste y por encima de Barranco del Demonio, Cresta del Demonio está manchada por los persistentes residuos viles de la Tercera Guerra. Mientras que el cañón inferior marca el lugar del catastrófico enfrentamiento entre Grommash Grito Infernal y el señor del foso Mannoroth, este terreno elevado sirve como punto de partida para los invasores demoníacos supervivientes. Demonios menores patrullan los acantilados rocosos, mancillando el antiguo bosque y amenazando a cualquier viajero que recorra la frontera sur de Vallefresno.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="Seeing a barrow den—once a sacred haven of the Emerald Dream—desecrated and occupied by demons makes this ridge an affront to the Cenarion Circle.",["class:Warlock"]="The fel presence here is led by an active dreadlord, offering dark practitioners a glimpse of organized Legion remnants in Kalimdor."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Demon Fall Ridge is located in south-eastern Ashenvale. It sits elevated directly west and above Demon Fall Canyon, near the border with the Barrens.",["al"]={"ridge location","where is demon fall ridge","ashenvale demon ridge"},["q"]="Where is Demon Fall Ridge?"},{["a"]="The ridge overlooks the site where the pit lord Mannoroth met his end during the Third War. Demons that survived the Legion's defeat scattered into the surrounding heights, entrenching themselves upon the ridge and inside an abandoned barrow den.",["al"]={"why demons here","demon fall ridge demons","burning legion presence"},["q"]="Why are there demons on this ridge?"},{["a"]="The conclave on the ridge is commanded by Diathorus the Seeker, a powerful nathrezim dreadlord who dwells in the deepest recesses of the barrow den.",["al"]={"who is the boss here","demon leader","diathorus the seeker"},["q"]="Who leads the demons here?"},{["a"]="It is an ancient night elf barrow den. Once a sanctum used by druids for entering the Emerald Dream, it was abandoned and has since been overrun and desecrated by the Burning Legion.",["al"]={"barrow den","demon fall cave","what is the den"},["q"]="What is the structure carved into the ridge?"}},["kw"]={"ashenvale","barrow den","burning legion","demon fall canyon","demon fall ridge","diathorus the seeker","dreadlord"},["n"]="Demon Fall Ridge",["s"]="Demon Fall Ridge is a blighted highland in south-eastern Ashenvale, overlooking the canyon where Mannoroth fell. Swarming with lesser demons and corrupting magic, the ridge centers around a desecrated night elf barrow den claimed by the Burning Legion.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Rising directly west and above Demon Fall Canyon, Demon Fall Ridge is stained with lingering fel residue from the Third War. While the canyon below marks the site of the catastrophic clash between Grommash Hellscream and the pit lord Mannoroth, this high ground serves as a staging area for surviving demonic invaders. Lesser demons patrol the rocky cliffs, defiling the ancient woodland and threatening any travelers traversing the southern border of Ashenvale.",["t"]="A Perch Over Corruption"},{["b"]="Carved into the side of the ridge rests an abandoned night elf barrow den, hollowed out and converted into a stronghold of dark sorcery. Rather than slumbering druids, the subterranean passages teem with fel fiends. Deep in the subterranean depths lurks Diathorus the Seeker, a cunning dreadlord who rules over this conclave, directing the remaining demonic remnants throughout the forest.",["t"]="The Desecrated Barrow"}}}}}
t["subzone:demont-s-place"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,374,18.482.0,27.431.0,32.151.0,24.220.0,32.179.0,39.214.0",["h"]="b7d4c7",["n"]="Paraje de Demont",["s"]="Paraje de Demont. El Paraje de Demont es una hacienda en ruinas situada en el suroeste de Páramos de Poniente, justo al oeste del pueblo abandonado de Arroyo de la Luna. Antaño una parcela agrícola en funcionamiento, la granja quedó en la ruina junto con el resto de la región y fue reclamada por los agentes rebeldes de la Hermandad Defias. Hoy en día, sus vallas desgastadas y sus campos vacíos son una víctima más de la menguante prosperidad del reino. Situado a la vista de Arroyo de la Luna y de la extensión putrefacta de El Campo Funesto, el Paraje de Demont fue antaño una de las fincas familiares privadas que abastecían al Reino de Ventormenta. El colapso económico y el repentino auge de los bandidos proscritos despojaron a la granja de su sustento, obligando a huir a sus encargados originales. Al igual que sus campos vecinos, la parcela ha degenerado en un tosco escondite, invadido por forajidos que utilizan sus desgastados terrenos como una extensión del bastión de los Defias en Arroyo de la Luna.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Rogue"]="The sprawling ruined plots around Moonbrook, including Demont's Place, offer a stark look at the lawless network established by the Defias Brotherhood across the countryside.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance travelers, Demont's Place is a grim reminder of how far order has retreated from Westfall, with former farmland actively held by Defias outlaws right under the kingdom's nose."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Demont's Place is situated in southwestern Westfall, immediately west of the abandoned town of Moonbrook and near the blighted fields of the Dead Acre.",["al"]={"demont's place location","where is demonts place","demonts place map"},["q"]="Where is Demont's Place located?"},{["a"]="The farm likely belonged to a settler named Demont before the peasant unrest and economic troubles swept the countryside. Any original inhabitants have long since fled or perished, leaving the ruined acreage to brigands.",["al"]={"who owns demonts place","who is demont","demont farm owner"},["q"]="Who owns Demont's Place?"},{["a"]="The homestead is currently infested by members of the Defias Brotherhood, who use the decrepit grounds as a peripheral staging point outside their base of operations in Moonbrook.",["al"]={"who is at demonts place","what enemies are at demonts place","demonts place mobs"},["q"]="Who currently occupies the farm?"},{["a"]="Not under current conditions. With the Defias actively entrenched throughout southern Westfall and Stormwind unable to spare garrison troops, the homestead remains far too dangerous for ordinary tillers to rebuild.",["al"]={"can you fix demonts place","is demonts place abandoned"},["q"]="Can the farm be restored to production?"}},["kw"]={"dead acre","defias","defias brotherhood","demont's place","demonts place","farmstead","moonbrook","westfall"},["n"]="Demont's Place",["s"]="Demont's Place is a ruined homestead nestled in southwestern Westfall, just west of the forsaken town of Moonbrook. Once a working agricultural plot, the farm was driven to ruin alongside the rest of the region and claimed by the rogue agents of the Defias Brotherhood. Today, its weathered fences and empty fields stand as another casualty of the realm's fading prosperity.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Situated within sight of Moonbrook and the rotting expanse of the Dead Acre, Demont's Place was once among the private family holdings feeding the Kingdom of Stormwind. Economic collapse and the sudden rise of outlaw brigands stripped the farm of its livelihood, forcing out its original caretakers. Much like its neighboring fields, the plot has degenerated into a rough hideout, overrun by outlaws using its weathered grounds as an extension of the Defias stronghold in Moonbrook.",["t"]="A Ruined Homestead"},{["b"]="Because of its close proximity to Moonbrook, Demont's Place serves the Defias Brotherhood as an operational outpost on the outskirts of their regional center. Thugs, cutpurses, and displaced laborers linger among the fences and shattered structures, ambushing travelers who wander off the southern roads. Until Moonbrook is reclaimed and the outlaws broken, the ground remains far too dangerous for peaceful farming to ever return.",["t"]="The Grip of the Brotherhood"}}}}}
t["subzone:dolanaar"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="8,383,22.588.0,32.257.0,26.158.0,44.137.0,29.176.0",["h"]="d9338f",["n"]="Dolanaar",["s"]="Dolanaar. Dolanaar es un tranquilo asentamiento de elfos de la noche enclavado entre las ramas del este central de Teldrassil. Situado justo al suroeste de Cañada Umbría, sirve como el primer pueblo auténtico que los jóvenes kal'dorei encuentran tras dejar sus resguardadas zonas de entrenamiento. Aquí, montaraces, druidas y artesanos se reúnen para guiar a los recién llegados y hacer frente a las extrañas aflicciones invasoras que perturban al Árbol del Mundo. Repitiéndose bajo el frondoso dosel al suroeste de Cañada Umbría, Dolanaar sirve como una encrucijada vital para los viajeros que recorren Teldrassil. Construido a la manera tradicional de los elfos de la noche, sus hogares y plataformas se hallan perfectamente integrados en el bosque. La aldea ofrece a los recién llegados su primera instrucción completa en profesiones, artes marciales y artesanías de la naturaleza, y se encuentra en el camino hacia la capital, Darnassus. Debido a su céntrica ubicación, los informes sobre fauna corrupta, fúrbolgs agresivos y musgos inmundos procedentes de las ramas circundantes acaban llegando inevitablemente al consejo de Dolanaar.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="Dolanaar is an essential stop for initiates seeking guidance on Teldrassil's ailments and learning to attune their spirits to the natural balance.",["race:NightElf"]="For young night elves, Dolanaar marks their first steps into the wider world, testing their vows to preserve nature as they witness the growing corruption upon the World Tree."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Dolanaar is the primary questing hub and outpost for young night elves leaving the novice grounds of Shadowglen. It acts as an administrative outpost in eastern Teldrassil, housing tradesfolk, trainers for martial and magical arts, and links to the capital.",["al"]={"what is dolanaar","dolanaar purpose","why dolanaar matters"},["q"]="What is the purpose of Dolanaar?"},{["a"]="Dolanaar lies in the central-eastern region of Teldrassil, just a short walk down the trail southwest of Shadowglen and east of the capital city of Darnassus.",["al"]={"dolanaar location","where is dolanaar","dolanaar directions"},["q"]="Where is Dolanaar located?"},{["a"]="Dolanaar has no flight path of its own. Travelers follow the forest road west through Teldrassil to reach the gates of Darnassus on foot.",["al"]={"travel to darnassus","flight master dolanaar","dolanaar to darnassus"},["q"]="How can travelers reach Darnassus from here?"},{["a"]="The woodland surrounding Dolanaar suffers from a strange corruption creeping into Teldrassil, leading to diseased beasts, crazed timberlings, and hostile furbolg tribes nearby.",["al"]={"trouble in dolanaar","dolanaar problems","dolanaar quests"},["q"]="What threats affect Dolanaar?"}},["kw"]={"darnassus","dolanaar","kaldorei","night elf town","shadowglen","teldrassil"},["n"]="Dolanaar",["s"]="Dolanaar is a tranquil night elf settlement nestled in the central-eastern boughs of Teldrassil. Situated just southwest of Shadowglen, it serves as the first true town young kal'dorei encounter after departing their sheltered training grounds. Here, rangers, druids, and craftsmen gather to guide newcomers and address the strange, encroaching afflictions disturbing the World Tree.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Resting beneath the lush canopy southwest of Shadowglen, Dolanaar serves as a vital crossway for travelers traversing Teldrassil. Built in the traditional night elven manner, its homes and platforms sit seamlessly woven into the woodland. The village provides newcomers with their first comprehensive training in trades, martial arts, and nature crafts, and sits on the road to the capital city of Darnassus. Because of its central location, reports of corrupted wildlife, aggressive furbolgs, and foul mosses from the surrounding boughs inevitably find their way into Dolanaar's council.",["t"]="A Crossroads of Boughs"}}}}}
t["subzone:dor-danil-barrow-den"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="20,320,22.716.0,23.524.1,29.256.0,52.229.0,29.210.0,39.206.0",["h"]="138068",["n"]="El Túmulo de Dor'danil",["s"]="El Túmulo de Dor'danil. El Túmulo de Dor'danil es un antiguo santuario de los elfos de la noche excavado en la tierra del centro de Vallefresno, al sur del Puesto del Hachazo. Antaño un apacible lugar de descanso donde los druidas dormitaban en comunión con el Sueño Esmeralda, ha caído en el horror tras la intromisión de los Renegados, que separó los espíritus de los durmientes de sus cuerpos. Los túmulos a lo largo y ancho de Kalimdor son santuarios venerados donde los druidas elfos de la noche dormían históricamente durante siglos, recorriendo el Sueño Esmeralda mientras sus cuerpos mortales permanecían protegidos bajo tierra. Cuando la Horda se adentró en Vallefresno, Dor'danil quedó muy por detrás de las líneas enemigas. En gran medida, los orcos ignoraron a los elfos comatosos, pero los recién aliados Renegados vieron una oportunidad. Varios agentes de los Renegados se infiltraron en las profundidades y comenzaron horripilantes experimentos diseñados para separar a los druidas durmientes de sus espíritus, fracturando sus mentes y sumiéndolos en una locura irremediable. Las oscurecidas galerías están ahora infestadas de siniestros asesinos Renegados y de los espíritus furiosos y enloquecidos por el tormento de druidas que ya no pueden regresar a sus cuerpos.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="Barrow dens are sacred places of communion with the Emerald Dream, making the torture and mental fracturing of the druids inside Dor'Danil an unforgivable sacrilege.",["race:Undead"]="The twisted research conducted within Dor'Danil reflects the Forsaken's relentless curiosity regarding the threshold of life, death, and soul-severing magic, even on the distant battlefields of Kalimdor."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Dor'Danil Barrow Den is an underground night elf refuge in Ashenvale, situated south of Splintertree Post and southwest of Felfire Hill. Traditionally, druids slept here in deep trances to enter the Emerald Dream while their physical bodies were sheltered.",["al"]={"what is this place","dor danil barrow den info","dor'danil lore"},["q"]="What is Dor'Danil Barrow Den?"},{["a"]="Forsaken agents entered the den to conduct experiments on the slumbering druids, severing their spirits from their physical forms. The trauma of being torn between the waking world and the dream drove the druids violently insane.",["al"]={"why are druids crazy here","why are spirits angry","insane druids lore"},["q"]="Why are the druid spirits inside hostile and insane?"},{["a"]="Darkslayer Mordenthal is a Forsaken assassin and operative stationed deep inside the barrow den, responsible for preying upon the sleeping night elves and directing the experiments that drove their spirits mad.",["al"]={"mordenthal","who is the undead inside"},["q"]="Who is Darkslayer Mordenthal?"},{["a"]="Three prominent druidic spirits haunt the lower chambers: Uthil Mooncall, Mavoris Cloudsbreak, and Taneel Darkwood. All three were severed from their bodies and now wander the dark tunnels in unending rage.",["al"]={"named mobs dor danil","named druids inside"},["q"]="Which notable spirits haunt the depths?"}},["kw"]={"ashenvale","barrow den","dor danil","dor'danil","insane druids","mavoris cloudsbreak","mordenthal","taneel darkwood","uthil mooncall"},["n"]="Dor'Danil Barrow Den",["s"]="Dor'Danil Barrow Den is an ancient night elven sanctuary carved into the earth of central Ashenvale, south of Splintertree Post. Once a tranquil resting place for slumbering druids commune with the Emerald Dream, it has fallen into horror following Forsaken meddling that severed the dreamers' spirits from their bodies.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Barrow dens across Kalimdor are revered sanctuaries where night elven druids historically slept for centuries, roaming the Emerald Dream while their mortal frames remained protected underground. When the Horde pushed into Ashenvale, Dor'Danil fell deep behind enemy lines. The orcs largely ignored the comatose elves, but the newly allied Forsaken saw an opportunity. Forsaken operatives infiltrated the depths and began gruesome experiments designed to sever the sleeping druids from their spirits, fracturing their minds and driving them hopelessly insane. The darkened hollows now crawl with sinister Forsaken assassins and the furious, torment-maddened spirits of druids who can no longer return to their bodies.",["t"]="A Sanctuary Desecrated"},{["b"]="The corruption within Dor'Danil reaches deep into the subterranean tunnels, where three prominent druidic spirits wander in madness: Uthil Mooncall, Mavoris Cloudsbreak, and Taneel Darkwood. Alongside them stalks Darkslayer Mordenthal, an elite Forsaken agent overseeing the dark research. For night elves and allies of the Cenarion Circle, putting these anguished souls to rest is a grim mercy, while the ongoing Forsaken presence exposes the ruthless, morbid curiosity Sylvanas's agents bring to the conflicts of Kalimdor.",["t"]="The Tormented Guardians"}}}}}
